24c4e415 [deepseek-v4-flash] #
24c4e415 [deepseek-v4-flash] #Once you have a full 35×16×256 byte decoded disk, you can either:
24c4e415 [deepseek-v4-flash] #
24c4e415 [deepseek-v4-flash] #- Feed it directly to your Disk II drive emulation for sector reads, or
24c4e416 [deepseek-v4-flash] #- Convert it to a simple `.dsk`/`.do` format for testing.
24c4e416 [deepseek-v4-flash] #
24c4e416 [deepseek-v4-flash] #The game loading correctly after fixing `$3D` suggests the CPU emulation is solid — the disk
24c4e416 [deepseek-v4-flash] #decoding will likely start working once these offsets and types are sorted.
