24ebfa1c [claude-haiku-4-5] #• Why games peek $D019:*
24ebfa1c [claude-haiku-4-5] #
24ebfa1d [claude-haiku-4-5] #1. Clear pending IRQ - Reading $D019 acknowledges/clears the interrupt flag
24ebfa1d [claude-haiku-4-5] #   - Bit 0: Raster compare IRQ occurred
24ebfa1d [claude-haiku-4-5] #   - Bit 1: Sprite-data collision
24ebfa1d [claude-haiku-4-5] #   - Bit 3: Light pen
24ebfa1d [claude-haiku-4-5] #   - Bit 7: IRQ signal active (read-only)
24ebfa1e [claude-haiku-4-5] #
24ebfa1e [claude-haiku-4-5] #2. Check IRQ status - Test which interrupt triggered
24ebfa1e [claude-haiku-4-5] #3. Interrupt handler protocol - Standard practice: IRQ handler reads $D019 to determine
24ebfa1f [claude-haiku-4-5] #cause, then clears it
24ebfa1f [claude-haiku-4-5] #
