24ecddfd [claude-haiku-4-5] #
24ecddfd [claude-haiku-4-5] #1. Selects row by writing to $9120 (Port B)
24ecddfe [claude-haiku-4-5] #   - Each bit represents a row: `EF`, `DF`, `BF`, `7F`, `$FF` (bits 4-7 active low)
24ecddfe [claude-haiku-4-5] #
24ecddfe [claude-haiku-4-5] #2. Reads column data from $9000 (Port A)
24ecddfe [claude-haiku-4-5] #   - Each bit in Port A represents a column (which key is pressed in that row)
24ecddff [claude-haiku-4-5] #   - Active low: `00` means key pressed, `FF` means no key in that row
24ecddff [claude-haiku-4-5] #
