 00\r\n[VIC] read via1_porta_keyboard_row 00\r\n[VIC] read via1_portb_cassette|joy BF\r\n[VIC(W)] PORTB 9120 7F\r\n[VIC] read via1_porta_keyboard_row 00\r\n[VIC] read via1_porta_keyboard_row 00\r\n[VIC] read via1_portb_cassette|joy 7F\r\n[VIC(W)] PORTB 9120 FF\r\n[VIC] read via1_porta_keyboard_row 00\r\n[VIC] read via1_porta_keyboard_row 00\r\n[VIC(W)] PORTB 9120 F7\r\n[VIC] read via2_latch1_lo 00\r\n[VIC] read PA_output 00\r\n[VIC] read PA_output 00\r\n[VIC] read via1_porta_cassette_sense 00\r\n[VIC] read via1_peripheral FC\r\n[VIC] read via1_interrupt_enable 82\r\n[VIC(W)] PCR 911C FC\r\n[VIC(W)] PORTB 9120 00\r\n[VIC] read via1_porta_keyboard_row 00\r\n[VIC(W)] PORTB 9120 FE\r\n[VIC] read via1_porta_keyboard_row 00\r\n[VIC] read via1_porta_keyboard_row 00\r\n","name":"content"},{"role":"user","content":"am testing vic20, display is very good\r\nFiles shared. Feel free to comment if content is new or different.","name":"simonsta"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Excellent! VIC-20 display working well. The notes show healthy keyboard scanning pattern (cycling through rows `$EF`, `$DF`, `$BF`, `$7F`, `$FF`) and cassette/joystick input handling.\n\n**What's working:**\n- VIA1 Port B keyboard row selection (`$9120`)\n- Port A keyboard input reads (`$9000`)\n- Interrupt enable register (`$911E`)\n- PCR (Peripheral Control Register) writes (`$911C`)\n\n**Minor observations from the trace:**\n\n1. **Keyboard scanning is good** — cycling through 8 rows properly\n2. **Latch reads** (`via2_latch1_lo`) — timer/counter logic firing\n3. **Cassette sense** always reads `$00` — tape input dormant (expected if no tape loaded)\n\n**If you want to refine further:**\n\nExtract platform-specific I/O into named helper functions to reduce code duplication:\n\n```typescript\nreadVIC20Register(address: number): number {\n\tswitch(address) {\n\t\tcase 0x9000: return this.readVIC20PortA();\n\t\tcase 0x9001: return this.readVIC20PortB();\n\t\tcase 0x911E: return this.memory[address]; // interrupt enable\n\t\tdefault: return this.memory[address];\n\t}\n}\n\nprivate readVIC20PortA(): number {\n\t// Keyboard matrix logic\n\treturn this.memory[0x9000];\n}\n```\n\nThe display quality is the real win here. Ship it! 🎯"},{"role":"user","content":"so to read keyboard it selects row and reads from where?","name":"simonsta"},{"role":"assistant","content":"**VIC-20 keyboard reading:**\n\nFrom your trace, the ROM code:\n\n1. **Selects row** by writing to **$9120** (Port B)\n   - Each bit represents a row: `$EF`, `$DF`, `$BF`, `$7F`, `$FF` (bits 4-7 active low)\n\n2. **Reads column data** from **$9000** (Port A)\n   - Each bit in Port A represents a column (which key is pressed in that row)\n   - Active low: `$00` means key pressed, `$FF` means no key in that row\n\n**Matrix example:**\n```\nWrite $EF to $9120  (select row 0)\nRead  $9000         (columns 0-7 for row 0)\n\nWrite $DF to $9120  (select row 1)\nRead  $9000         (columns 0-7 for row 1)\n\n... etc for all 8 rows\n```\n\n**In your code, you're reading:**\n```typescript\n[VIC] read via1_porta_keyboard_row 00  ← Port A at $9000\n```\n\nSo your emulator is correctly returning from `$9000`, but you need to implement the **keyboard matrix lookup**. Currently returning `00` always suggests no keys pressed (or matrix not implemented).\n\n**To implement:**\n\n```typescript\nreadVIC20PortA(): number {\n\tconst selectedRow = this.memory[0x9120] ^ 0xFF; // invert for active-low\n\tconst rowIndex = Math.log2(selectedRow & 0xF0) - 4;\n\t\n\t// Return column bits for this row from actual keypress state\n\treturn this.keyboardMatrix[rowIndex] ?? 0xFF;\n}\n```\n\nDoes your emulator track keypresses in a matrix array?"},{"role":"user","content":"what is first key of first column in vic20?","name":"simonsta"},{"role":"assistant","content":"**VIC-20 keyboard matrix - Row 0, Column 0 (bit 0 of Port A when $9120 = $EF):**\n\n**`1` key** (the number one)\n\n**Full Row 0 layout ($9120 = $EF):**\n```\nBit 0 ($01): 1\nBit 1 ($02): 2\nBit 2 ($04): 3\nBit 3 ($08): 4\nBit 4 ($10): 5\nBit 5 ($20): 6\nBit 6 ($40): 7\nBit 7 ($80): 8\n```\n\nWhen key `1` is pressed, reading `$9000` should return `$FE` (bit 0 clear, others set—active low).\n\nYour trace shows `$00` always, which means either:\n- No keyboard matrix implemented yet\n- All keys reading as pressed simultaneously\n- Matrix not wired to actual keypress tracking\n\nDoes your `onInput()` function populate a keyboard matrix when keys are pressed?"},{"role":"user","content":"{\"path\":\"C:\\\\nitrologic\\\\arcade\\\\machine.ts\",\"length\":109529,\"type\":\"text/x-typescript\",\"tag\":\"\"}","name":"blob"},{"role":"user","content":"// machine.ts\r\n// (c) 2026 nitrologic\r\n// All Rights Reserved\r\n\r\nimport { unZip } from \"./unzip.ts\";\r\nimport { parseWavHeader, parseWavFile, writeWavFile } from \"./wavfileutil.ts\";\r\n\r\nimport mos6502 from \"./mos6502.json\" with { type: \"json\" };\r\nimport vic20 from \"./commodore/vic20.json\" with { type: \"json\" };\r\nimport vic1541 from \"./commodore/vic1541.json\" with { type: \"json\" };\r\nimport plus4 from \"./commodore/plus4.json\" with { type: \"json\" };\r\nimport c64 from \"./commodore/c64.json\" with { type: \"json\" };\r\nimport atari0 from \"./atari/atarilunarlanderrev4.json\" with { type: \"json\" };\r\nimport atari1 from \"./atari/ataricentipederev4.json\" with { type: \"json\" };\r\nimport atari2 from \"./atari/atariasteroidsrev4.json\" with { type: \"json\" };\r\nimport atari3 from \"./atari/ataribattlezonerev2.json\" with { type: \"json\" };\r\nimport apple2 from \"./apple/appleII.json\" with { type: \"json\" };\r\nimport apple2plus from \"./apple/appleIIplus.json\" with { type: \"json\" };\r\n\r\nimport appleSabotage from \"./apple/applesabotage.json\" with { type: \"json\" };\r\nimport applePennyArcade from \"./apple/applepennyarcade.json\" with { type: \"json\" };\r\nimport appleElite from \"./apple/appleelite.json\" with { type: \"json\" };\r\n\r\nconst machineROMs=[\r\n\tvic20,vic1541,c64,plus4,\r\n\tapple2plus,apple2,\r\n\tatari0,atari1,atari2,atari3\r\n];\r\n\r\nconst machineSpec=vic20;//apple2plus;//c64;//apple2;//plus4;//plus4;//c64;//apple2plus;//atari0;//apple2plus;//atari0;//apple2;//atari2;//await select(roms);\r\n\r\nconst appleGames=[appleElite,appleSabotage,applePennyArcade];\r\n\r\nimport { sleep, isRunning, stopRunning, runTerminal, pollKeypad, pollTerminal, stopTerminal } from \"./terminalarcade.ts\";\r\nimport console from \"node:console\";\r\n\r\nconst machineTitle=\"machine 1.5 (c) 2026 nitrologic\";\r\n\r\nlet running=true;\r\nlet stepping=false;\r\nlet tracing=false;\r\n\r\n/*\r\nconst unit8=new Machine();\r\nunit8.burn(vic1541.rom);\r\nconst id=parseInt(vic1541.address.ID,16);\r\nconst version=parseInt(vic1541.address.VERSION,16);\r\nconst idString=unit8.peekString(id);\r\nconst v65=unit8.memory[version]; // enforce value is A (65) \r\nconsole.log(vic1541.title,idString,(v65==65)?\"A\":\"???\");\r\nconst game=unit8;\r\nconst gameRom=vic1541;\r\n*/\r\n\r\nconst gameRom=machineSpec;\r\nconst platform=machineSpec.platform;\r\n\r\nlet is1541=false;\r\nlet isVIC=(platform==\"vic20\");\r\nlet isTed=(platform==\"plus4\");\r\nlet isApple=(platform==\"appleii\");\r\nlet isC64=(platform==\"c64\");\r\nlet isAtari=false;\r\n\r\n// global inputs from processInput() courtesy terminalarcade\r\n\r\nlet hitBits=0;\r\nlet hitCount=0;\r\n\r\nlet mouseX=0;\r\nlet mouseY=0;\r\n\r\nlet axisY=0;\r\nlet axisX=0;\r\n\r\nlet clicks=0;\r\n\r\nlet rasterLine=0;\r\n\r\nconst CyclesPerLine=60;\r\n\r\n\r\nconst cusorPasteOn=\"\\x1b[?2004h\";\r\nconst cusorPasteOff=\"\\x1b[?2004l\";\r\n\r\nconst cursorYellow=\"\\x1b[43m\";\r\nconst cursorGreen=\"\\x1b[42m\";\r\n\r\nconst cursorPlain=\"\\x1b[0m\";\r\nconst cursorBold=\"\\x1b[1m\";\r\nconst cursorSave=\"\\x1b[s\";\r\nconst cursorRestore=\"\\x1b[u\";\r\nconst cursorHome=\"\\x1b[H\";\r\nconst cursorErase=\"\\x1b[K\";\r\nconst cursorClear=\"\\x1b[2J\\x1b[1;1H\";\r\nconst cursorUp=\"\\x1b[A\";\r\nconst cursorDown=\"\\x1b[B\";\r\nconst cursorHide=\"\\x1b[?25l\";\r\nconst cursorShow=\"\\x1b[?25h\";\r\n\r\nfunction cursorPos(x:number,y:number):string{\r\n\treturn \"\\x1b[\"+(y||1)+\";\"+(x||1)+\"H\";\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction cursorHor(x:number):string{\r\n\treturn \"\\x1b[\"+(x||1)+\"G\";\r\n}\r\n\r\nconst POKEY_RANDOM=0x100a;\r\n\r\nconsole.log(machineTitle);\r\n\r\n//console.log(cursorClear+machineTitle);\r\n//console.log(mos6502.name,mos6502.version,mos6502.copyright);\r\n\r\n// each char is two 16 color blocks high\r\n// ansi fg,bg to set colors for each 1x2 char\r\n\r\nconst appleBlock=new Array<string>(256);\r\n\r\nconst appleANSI = [\r\n\t16,  // 0 Black\r\n\t197, // 1 Deep Pink\r\n\t61,  // 2 Medium Slate Blue\r\n\t201, // 3 Magenta\r\n\t22,  // 4 Dark Green\t// was 28\r\n\t244, // 5 Gray\r\n\t39,  // 6 Deep Sky Blue\r\n\t147, // 7 Light Periwinkle\r\n\t94,  // 8 Dark Goldenrod\r\n\t208, // 9 Dark Orange\r\n\t250, // 10 Light Gray\r\n\t218, // 11 Light Pink\r\n\t46,  // 12 Lime\r\n\t190, // 13 Chartreuse\r\n\t123, // 14 Aquamarine\r\n\t231, // 15 White\r\n];\r\n\r\nconst tedANSI = [\r\n\t16,  // 0 Black\r\n\t255, // 1 White\r\n\t131, // 2 Red\r\n\t116, // 3 Cyan\r\n\t133, // 4 Purple\r\n\t71,  // 5 Green\r\n\t26,  // 6 Blue\r\n\t227, // 7 Yellow\r\n\t172, // 8 Orange\r\n\t94,  // 9 Brown\r\n\t174, // 10 Light Red\r\n\t240, // 11 Dark Gray\r\n\t246, // 12 Medium Gray\r\n\t120, // 13 Light Green\r\n\t111, // 14 Light Blue\r\n\t250, // 15 Light Gray\r\n];\r\n\r\nconst c64ANSI = [\r\n\t16,  // 0 Black\r\n\t231, // 1 White\r\n\t131, // 2 Red\r\n\t116, // 3 Cyan\r\n\t133, // 4 Purple\r\n\t71,  // 5 Green\r\n\t26,  // 6 Blue\r\n\t227, // 7 Yellow\r\n\t172, // 8 Orange\r\n\t94,  // 9 Brown\r\n\t174, // 10 Light Red\r\n\t238, // 11 Dark Gray\r\n\t244, // 12 Medium Gray\r\n\t120, // 13 Light Green\r\n\t111, // 14 Light Blue\r\n\t250, // 15 Light Gray\r\n];\r\nconst vic20ANSI = [\r\n\t16,  // 0  Black\r\n\t231, // 1  White\r\n\t131, // 2  Red\r\n\t116, // 3  Cyan\r\n\t133, // 4  Purple\r\n\t71,  // 5  Green\r\n\t26,  // 6  Blue\r\n\t186, // 7  Yellow          (slightly different from C64)\r\n\t172, // 8  Orange\r\n\t180, // 9  Light Orange\r\n\t174, // 10 Light Red / Pink\r\n\t159, // 11 Light Cyan\r\n\t177, // 12 Light Purple\r\n\t120, // 13 Light Green\r\n\t111, // 14 Light Blue\r\n\t229, // 15 Light Yellow\r\n];\r\n\r\nconst textColors=15+64;\r\n\r\nfunction initAppleBlocks(){\r\n\tfor(let i=0;i<256;i++){\r\n\t\tconst lo=appleANSI[i&15];\r\n\t\tconst hi=appleANSI[i>>4];\r\n\t\tconst block=\"\\x1b[38;5;\"+lo+\"m\\x1b[48;5;\"+hi+\"m▀\";\r\n\t\tappleBlock[i]=block;\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction appleColor(i:number):string{\r\n\tconst lo=appleANSI[i&15];\r\n\tconst hi=appleANSI[i>>4];\r\n\tconst code=\"\\x1b[38;5;\"+lo+\"m\\x1b[48;5;\"+hi+\"m\";\r\n\treturn code;\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction c64Color(i:number):string{\r\n\tconst lo=c64ANSI[i&15];\r\n\tconst hi=c64ANSI[i>>4];\r\n\tconst code=\"\\x1b[38;5;\"+lo+\"m\\x1b[48;5;\"+hi+\"m\";\r\n\treturn code;\r\n}\r\nfunction vic20Color(i:number):string{\r\n\tconst lo=vic20ANSI[i&15];\r\n\tconst hi=vic20ANSI[i>>4];\r\n\tconst code=\"\\x1b[38;5;\"+lo+\"m\\x1b[48;5;\"+hi+\"m\";\r\n\treturn code;\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction tedColor(i:number):string{\r\n\tconst lo=tedANSI[i&15];\r\n\tconst hi=tedANSI[i>>4];\r\n\tconst code=\"\\x1b[38;5;\"+lo+\"m\\x1b[48;5;\"+hi+\"m\";\r\n\treturn code;\r\n}\r\n\r\n// 280x192 hires mode279-c\r\nconst braille=[\r\n    \"⠀⠁⠂⠃⠄⠅⠆⠇⠈⠉⠊⠋⠌⠍⠎⠏⠐⠑⠒⠓⠔⠕⠖⠗⠘⠙⠚⠛⠜⠝⠞⠟⠠⠡⠢⠣⠤⠥⠦⠧⠨⠩⠪⠫⠬⠭⠮⠯⠰⠱⠲⠳⠴⠵⠶⠷⠸⠹⠺⠻⠼⠽⠾⠿\",\r\n    \"⡀⡁⡂⡃⡄⡅⡆⡇⡈⡉⡊⡋⡌⡍⡎⡏⡐⡑⡒⡓⡔⡕⡖⡗⡘⡙⡚⡛⡜⡝⡞⡟⡠⡡⡢⡣⡤⡥⡦⡧⡨⡩⡪⡫⡬⡭⡮⡯⡰⡱⡲⡳⡴⡵⡶⡷⡸⡹⡺⡻⡼⡽⡾⡿\",\r\n    \"⢀⢁⢂⢃⢄⢅⢆⢇⢈⢉⢊⢋⢌⢍⢎⢏⢐⢑⢒⢓⢔⢕⢖⢗⢘⢙⢚⢛⢜⢝⢞⢟⢠⢡⢢⢣⢤⢥⢦⢧⢨⢩⢪⢫⢬⢭⢮⢯⢰⢱⢲⢳⢴⢵⢶⢷⢸⢹⢺⢻⢼⢽⢾⢿\",\r\n    \"⣀⣁⣂⣃⣄⣅⣆⣇⣈⣉⣊⣋⣌⣍⣎⣏⣐⣑⣒⣓⣔⣕⣖⣗⣘⣙⣚⣛⣜⣝⣞⣟⣠⣡⣢⣣⣤⣥⣦⣧⣨⣩⣪⣫⣬⣭⣮⣯⣰⣱⣲⣳⣴⣵⣶⣷⣸⣹⣺⣻⣼⣽⣾⣿\"];\r\n\r\nfunction displayHires(mem:Uint8Array,frameCount:number,mode:number){\r\n\tconst base=(mode&Page2Mode)?0x4000:0x2000;\r\n\tfor(let y=0;y<192;y+=4){\r\n\t\tconst line=[appleColor(8)];\r\n\t\tconst offset=base + ((y&7)<<10) + 128*((y>>3)&7) + 40*(y>>6);\r\n\t\tfor(let x=0;x<40;x+=2){\r\n\t\t\tconst b00=mem[offset+x];\r\n\t\t\tconst b01=mem[offset+x+1];\r\n\t\t\tconst b10=mem[offset+x+1024];\r\n\t\t\tconst b11=mem[offset+x+1025];\r\n\t\t\tconst b20=mem[offset+x+2048];\r\n\t\t\tconst b21=mem[offset+x+2049];\r\n\t\t\tconst b30=mem[offset+x+3072];\r\n\t\t\tconst b31=mem[offset+x+3073];\r\n\t\t\tlet b0=(b01<<7)|(b00&0x7f);\r\n\t\t\tlet b1=(b11<<7)|(b10&0x7f);\r\n\t\t\tlet b2=(b21<<7)|(b20&0x7f);\r\n\t\t\tlet b3=(b31<<7)|(b30&0x7f);\r\n            for(let i=0;i<7;i++){\r\n                const b50=\r\n                    ((b0&1)<<0)|\r\n                    ((b1&1)<<1)|\r\n                    ((b2&1)<<2)|\r\n                    ((b0&2)<<2)|\r\n                    ((b1&2)<<3)|\r\n                    ((b2&2)<<4);\r\n                line.push(braille[b3&3][b50]);\r\n                b0>>=2;b1>>=2;b2>>=2;b3>>=2;\r\n\t\t\t}\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tconsole.log(line.join(\"\"));\r\n\t}\r\n\tconsole.log(cursorPlain+cursorHome);\r\n}\r\n\r\nconst GraphicsMode=1;\r\nconst MixedMode=2;\r\nconst HiresMode=4;\r\nconst Page2Mode=8;\r\n\r\n\r\nconst fullWidth =\r\n  \"　\" +                          // 32 space\r\n  \"！＂＃＄％＆＇（）＊＋，－．／\" + // 33-47\r\n  \"０１２３４５６７８９\" +         // 48-57\r\n  \"：；＜＝＞？＠\" +               // 58-64\r\n  \"ＡＢＣＤＥＦＧＨＩＪＫＬＭＮＯＰＱＲＳＴＵＶＷＸＹＺ\" + // 65-90\r\n  \"［＼］＾＿｀\" +                 // 91-96\r\n  \"ａｂｃｄｅｆｇｈｉｊｋｌｍｎｏｐｑｒｓｔｕｖｗｘｙｚ\" + // 97-122\r\n  \"｛｜｝～\";                     // 123-126\r\n\r\nconst petsciiUppercase =\r\n  \"@ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ[$]↑←\"+\r\n  \" !\\\"#$%&'()*+,-./0123456789:;<=>?-\"+\r\n  \"♠│━╮╰╯╱╲◢◣◥┼▕◢◤◥╳↑╱╲╲│━╮╰╯\" + // 65-90: Graphic glyphs mapped to Shifted A-Z\r\n  \"│━▔▕━◥▏▒▕▔▒▒▬▔▒▎▍▒▒▔▕░▒▓█\" + // 91-116: C64 symbols\r\n  \"▊▕▬▕▔▎▍▒▕▔▒▒▬▔▒\"; // 117-127: C64 symbols\r\n\r\n  const petsciiUppercaseWide =\r\n  \"＠\" + // 0: @\r\n  \"ＡＢＣＤＥＦＧＨＩＪＫＬＭＮＯＰＱＲＳＴＵＶＷＸＹＺ\" + // 1-26: A-Z\r\n  \"［￡］↑←\" + // 27-31: [, £, ], ↑, ←\r\n  \"　\" + // 32: Space\r\n  \"！＂＃＄％＆＇（）＊＋，－．／\" + // 33-47\r\n  \"０１２３４５６７８９\" + // 