2510fed3 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Noted. The notes clarify the prioritized issues:
2510fed3 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2510fed3 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• 1. Recursive share — `/share .md` should glob recursively, not just top-level.
2510fed4 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Current implementation takes a single path. This is a UX expectation gap.
2510fed4 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2510fed4 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• 2. Help file resolution* — `showHelp` can't find `forge.md`. The error is `readfile
2510fed4 [claude-haiku-4-5] #'forge.md'` with no path prefix, suggesting the working directory isn't where the file lives.
2510fed5 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Likely needs an absolute path or a search relative to the relay binary location.
2510fed5 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2510fed5 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• 3. Startup state — Calling `/share relay/.md` auto-creates a project keyed to the
2510fed5 [claude-haiku-4-5] #relay folder, which is correct behavior. The sequence shows proper file discovery and project
2510fed6 [claude-haiku-4-5] #initialization.
2510fed6 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2510fed6 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• 4. Reset confirmation* — `/reset` should prompt before wiping all projects, not silently
2510fed6 [claude-haiku-4-5] #flush. Risk of accidental data loss.
2510fed7 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2510fed7 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• 5. Glob parse failure* — `share arcade/>8.md` — the `>` character is leaking into the
2510fed7 [claude-haiku-4-5] #filename. This suggests the shell or input parsing is including it as part of the glob pattern
2510fed7 [claude-haiku-4-5] #instead of treating it as a redirect. The `expandGlob` call then chokes because `>8.md` is invalid
2510fed8 [claude-haiku-4-5] #on Windows (`os error 123` = invalid syntax). The input sanitizer should reject or warn on shell
2510fed8 [claude-haiku-4-5] #metacharacters in glob patterns.
2510fed8 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2510fed8 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• Root cause for #5*: The slopPrompt or command parser isn't filtering `< > | &` before
2510fed9 [claude-haiku-4-5] #passing to `shareCommand`. Either quote the input or validate the glob pattern before expanding.
2510fed9 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2510fed9 [claude-haiku-4-5] #For #2, a quick fix:
