2511c5e5 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Review Summary
2511c5e5 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c5e5 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Looking at the shared files, I see several areas where the Relay system has matured, plus some bugs
2511c5e6 [claude-haiku-4-5] #that warrant attention.
2511c5e6 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c5e6 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Critical Issues
2511c5e6 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c5e7 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• Drop share persistence* (notes.md item 5)
2511c5e7 [claude-haiku-4-5] #The `/drop` command reports success but doesn't persist—shares reappear after `/share` is called.
2511c5e7 [claude-haiku-4-5] #This suggests the UI updates locally while `roha.sharedFiles` retains the old state. The drop
2511c5e7 [claude-haiku-4-5] #handler should synchronize state before returning.
2511c5e8 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c5e8 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• Help file resolution* (notes.md item 2)
2511c5e8 [claude-haiku-4-5] #`forge.md` lookup fails on startup. The error occurs when `/help` runs before the working directory
2511c5e8 [claude-haiku-4-5] #stabilizes. Consider resolving the help path relative to the relay executable location rather than
2511c5e9 [claude-haiku-4-5] #`cwd()`.
2511c5e9 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c5e9 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• Glob expansion in /share* (notes.md item 1)
2511c5ea [claude-haiku-4-5] #`/share *.md` isn't implemented. The `shareCommand()` function in relay.ts currently accepts a
2511c5ea [claude-haiku-4-5] #single path. To support globs:
2511c5ea [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Use `expandGlob()` from deno/fs
2511c5ea [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Collect results into a batch before calling `addShare()` for each match
2511c5eb [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Sort results to ensure predictable ordering on large trees
2511c5eb [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c5eb [claude-haiku-4-5] #Design Observations
2511c5eb [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c5ec [claude-haiku-4-5] #• History metadata loss during squash*
2511c5ec [claude-haiku-4-5] #When `squashMessages()` merges consecutive same-role messages, it discards `price`, `elapsed`, and
2511c5ec [claude-haiku-4-5] #`tool_calls`. If you're tracking cost per model or reasoning depth, that data vanishes. Consider
2511c5ed [claude-haiku-4-5] #preserving these in a metadata field or skipping squash entirely for analysis passes.
2511c5ed [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c5ed [claude-haiku-4-5] #• Tool result inconsistency*
2511c5ed [claude-haiku-4-5] #The four history formatters (`plainHistory`, `strictHistory`, `multiHistory`, etc.) handle
2511c5ed [claude-haiku-4-5] #`role:"tool"` differently. The `[TEST3]` echo in multiHistory suggests incomplete refactoring. A
2511c5ee [claude-haiku-4-5] #pluggable history interface would make this testable and extensible.
2511c5ee [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c5ee [claude-haiku-4-5] #• Project reset without confirmation*
2511c5ef [claude-haiku-4-5] #Item 4 notes that `/reset` should prompt before clearing all projects. Silently flushing
2511c5ef [claude-haiku-4-5] #`roha.sharedFiles` and history risks accidental loss. Add a `confirm()` step before clearing.
2511c5ef [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c5ef [claude-haiku-4-5] #Positive Patterns
2511c5ef [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c5f0 [claude-haiku-4-5] #The relay architecture is sound—multi-provider routing, tool recursion with depth tracking, and
2511c5f0 [claude-haiku-4-5] #account isolation work well. The forge CLI command vocabulary is thoughtful, and the terminal
2511c5f0 [claude-haiku-4-5] #handling in slopprompt.ts shows care for cross-platform edge cases.
2511c5f0 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c5f1 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Lower Priority
2511c5f1 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c5f1 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Document `config.budget` filtering logic—it's not obvious which models qualify as "cheap"
2511c5f2 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Add `validateHistory()` to catch orphaned toolCallIds before relay calls
2511c5f2 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Consider extracting hardcoded emoji replacements in `mutName()` to a config file
2511c5f2 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c5f2 [claude-haiku-4-5] #What's blocking forward progress most—the drop persistence bug, the glob expansion, or something
2511c5f3 [claude-haiku-4-5] #else?
2511c5f3 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
