2511c88d [claude-haiku-4-5] #biblispec Review
2511c88e [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c88e [claude-haiku-4-5] #The biblispec project is a well-curated reference for Unicode, typography, and linguistic systems.
2511c88e [claude-haiku-4-5] #Several observations:
2511c88e [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c88f [claude-haiku-4-5] #Strong Design
2511c88f [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c88f [claude-haiku-4-5] #• Structural clarity* — The JSON organization (books/, biblispec.json as payload) is sound.
2511c88f [claude-haiku-4-5] #Separating concerns like machine specs, audio circuits, and phrases into modular JSON files keeps
2511c890 [claude-haiku-4-5] #the payload navigable.
2511c890 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c890 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• Unicode scholarship* — The Egyptian Hieroglyphic coverage (1072 codepoints across
2511c890 [claude-haiku-4-5] #U+1300–U+1342) is thorough. The categorical breakdown (Women, Eyes, Fish, Birds, Animals) makes the
2511c891 [claude-haiku-4-5] #block approachable. Similar care shown in Alchemical symbols, Ogham, Cherokee, Vai, and CJK
2511c891 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Enclosed Digits.
2511c891 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c892 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• Linguistic breadth* — Hebrew, Coptic, Greek, Latin, Reo Māori, Linear B—each with
2511c892 [claude-haiku-4-5] #alphabet data (lower, upper, uncommon variants). Practical for text processing pipelines.
2511c892 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c892 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Content Observations
2511c892 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c893 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• "Labyrinthine typography" in scratch.md* — The discussion of Escher-style interlocking
2511c893 [claude-haiku-4-5] #graffiti (tessellation, Penrose illusion, mechanical wildstyle) is creative but feels orphaned.
2511c893 [claude-haiku-4-5] #This reads like research notes. Consider either:
2511c893 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Expanding it into a proper spec subsection (e.g., `books/typography.json` with glyph tessellation
2511c894 [claude-haiku-4-5] #rules)
2511c894 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Removing it if it's exploratory scaffolding
2511c894 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c895 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• Array vs. Class skirmish* — You note the conflict in machinespec.json (ordered arrays
2511c895 [claude-haiku-4-5] #like `software-architecture: [...]` vs. keyed objects like `video-game: {Speed Race: {...}}`). This
2511c895 [claude-haiku-4-5] #is genuine design tension:
2511c895 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Arrays preserve insertion order and support iteration
2511c896 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Objects allow semantic keys and O(1) lookup
2511c896 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Mixed use forces consumers to check type at runtime
2511c896 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c896 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Consider standardizing: either all keyed objects with a `_order` metadata array, or all arrays with
2511c897 [claude-haiku-4-5] #a `key` property on each item.
2511c897 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c897 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• pheme word building* — The prefix/suffix system (pre62, suff27) is linguistically sound
2511c897 [claude-haiku-4-5] #but underdocumented. What's the difference between "pre62" and the 61 listed? Are there conflicting
2511c898 [claude-haiku-4-5] #phemes across categories?
2511c898 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c898 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Missing Pieces
2511c898 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c899 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• "Fenced for inspections" geometry* — The character sets (pointChars, starChars, boxChars,
2511c899 [claude-haiku-4-5] #etc.) are useful, but no accompanying metadata. Consider adding:
2511c899 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Unicode block ranges (e.g., Box Drawing is U+2500–U+257F)
2511c899 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Rendering width (monospace width assumptions)
2511c89a [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Terminal compatibility notes (some terminals mangle box chars)
2511c89a [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c89a [claude-haiku-4-5] #• Chord notation clarity* — The "Sound of Silence" example uses `Dm...C...|Dm.F.BbF` with
2511c89a [claude-haiku-4-5] #dots and pipes, but the system isn't formally defined. How many beats per dot? What's the measure
2511c89b [claude-haiku-4-5] #structure exactly? (You mention 4,4,6 phrasing but show standard 4/4 chords.)
2511c89b [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c89b [claude-haiku-4-5] #• docs/ folder PDF strategy* — You've added the EDVAC report. The roadmap isn't clear: are
2511c89b [claude-haiku-4-5] #you archiving all historical specs, or just landmarks? A manifest with publication dates and
2511c89c [claude-haiku-4-5] #relevance would help future maintenance.
2511c89c [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c89c [claude-haiku-4-5] #Integration Notes
2511c89d [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c89d [claude-haiku-4-5] #The biblispec works well as a reference data layer for Slop Fountain and Relay. The emoji
2511c89d [claude-haiku-4-5] #width cludges in slopprompt.ts could be replaced with queries against `biblispec.unicode` to make
2511c89d [claude-haiku-4-5] #terminal rendering more consistent.
2511c89e [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511c89e [claude-haiku-4-5] #For the next round, I'd recommend:
2511c89e [claude-haiku-4-5] #1. Settle the array/object variance—pick one idiom
2511c89e [claude-haiku-4-5] #2. Formalize the chord notation syntax (or link to a standard)
2511c89f [claude-haiku-4-5] #3. Extract the tessellation typography notes into either a proper spec or a separate "research/"
2511c89f [claude-haiku-4-5] #folder
2511c89f [claude-haiku-4-5] #4. Add Unicode block metadata to fenced geometry sets
2511c89f [claude-haiku-4-5] #
