2511d203 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Arcade Project Review
2511d204 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511d204 [claude-haiku-4-5] #The arcade emulation work is coherent and well-scoped. Several observations:
2511d204 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511d204 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Strong Technical Foundation
2511d204 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511d205 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• POKEY register documentation* — Comprehensive pinout (40 pins), interrupt map, and shadow
2511d205 [claude-haiku-4-5] #RAM addresses. The dual-use addressing (e.g., `$D200` as AUDF1 write, POT0 read) is clearly laid
2511d205 [claude-haiku-4-5] #out. This will be essential when wiring keyboard and paddle input into the emulator.
2511d205 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511d206 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• DVG opcode reference* — Clean breakdown of the Atari vector generator. The SVEC
2511d206 [claude-haiku-4-5] #description (2-byte compressed format with scale, X/Y deltas, brightness) is precise. The state
2511d206 [claude-haiku-4-5] #machine (LABS → VCTR/SVEC → JSRL/RTSL → HALT) matches the hardware protocol.
2511d206 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511d207 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• Mixtape datasette spec* — Using RIFF chunks (fmt, cue, LIST, data) for cassette metadata
2511d207 [claude-haiku-4-5] #is pragmatic. The spec targets AppleII and VIC20, which makes sense for vintage emulation. The
2511d207 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Mathematical Alphanumeric Symbols styling (sans-bold digits `𝟬𝟭𝟮`) is a nice touch for UI
2511d207 [claude-haiku-4-5] #rendering.
2511d208 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511d208 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Gaps and Concerns
2511d208 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511d208 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• README.md is incomplete* — The file contains only character definitions copied from
2511d209 [claude-haiku-4-5] #biblispec (colorChars, pointChars, etc.). No project description, no emulator roadmap, no machine
2511d209 [claude-haiku-4-5] #targets listed. This should document:
2511d209 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Which machines are under emulation (Atari 2600? Centipede arcade board? Apple II?)
2511d209 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Current emulation state (CPU only? Graphics? Audio?)
2511d20a [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Build/run instructions
2511d20a [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511d20a [claude-haiku-4-5] #• POKEY missing implementation notes* — The register table is reference-grade, but there's
2511d20a [claude-haiku-4-5] #no guidance on emulation priority:
2511d20b [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Which channels matter first (audio vs. keyboard)?
2511d20b [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Paddle timing (the 8-bit timer resolution—how accurate does it need to be)?
2511d20b [claude-haiku-4-5] #- High-pass filter behavior between channels (is this critical for audio accuracy, or cosmetic?)
2511d20b [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Serial I/O (needed for the emulator scope, or can it be stubbed?)
2511d20b [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511d20c [claude-haiku-4-5] #• DVG implementation incomplete* — vectorgenerator.md describes opcodes but lacks:
2511d20c [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Scale calculation rules (how does `SSSS` from SVEC multiply against global scale from LABS?)
2511d20c [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Drawing primitive (how are X/Y deltas converted to screen coordinates?)
2511d20c [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Subroutine stack depth (how deep can JSRL nest before stack exhaustion?)
2511d20c [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Timing model (do all opcodes consume the same cycles, or does VCTR take longer than SVEC?)
2511d20d [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511d20d [claude-haiku-4-5] #• Mixtape spec underdeveloped* — The RIFF structure is defined, but:
2511d20d [claude-haiku-4-5] #- No byte layout for the `cue ` chunk (offset format, slot count, etc.)
2511d20d [claude-haiku-4-5] #- No `LIST` chunk schema for slot labels
2511d20e [claude-haiku-4-5] #- No ID3 or DISP chunk encoding details (referenced in wavfileutil.ts excerpt but not documented)
2511d20e [claude-haiku-4-5] #- No example WAV file or test vectors
2511d20e [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511d20e [claude-haiku-4-5] #Integration with Relay/Fountain
2511d20f [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511d20f [claude-haiku-4-5] #The arcade project maps naturally into the Slop Fountain ecosystem:
2511d20f [claude-haiku-4-5] #- biblispec provides the character sets for UI rendering (boxChars, arrowChars for display
2511d20f [claude-haiku-4-5] #frames)
2511d20f [claude-haiku-4-5] #- relay can manage emulator state, load/save game snapshots via `/project`
2511d210 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- mixtape datasette becomes a versioned cassette format for sharing game recordings
2511d210 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2511d210 [claude-haiku-4-5] #However, the three projects (relay, biblispec, arcade) are loosely coupled. Consider:
2511d210 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- A shared `machines.json` in biblispec listing Atari 2600, Centipede, Apple II specs (CPU, RAM,
2511d211 [claude-haiku-4-5] #ROM addresses, I/O map)
2511d211 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Arcade emulator consuming this as initialization config
2511d211 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Relay `/dump` command exposing emulator machine profiles
2511d211 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
