25124df9 [claude-haiku-4-5] #VIDBIT Hardware Integration
25124dfa [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25124dfa [claude-haiku-4-5] #Good hardware reference docs. A few observations on the connector mapping:
25124dfa [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25124dfa [claude-haiku-4-5] #Pinout Notes
25124dfb [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25124dfb [claude-haiku-4-5] #• PS/2 Mini DIN 6* — Standard layout, but worth confirming:
25124dfb [claude-haiku-4-5] #- GP0/GP1 for data/clock makes sense (input capture)
25124dfb [claude-haiku-4-5] #- GP2/GP3 for UART rx/tx is clean isolation
25124dfc [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25124dfc [claude-haiku-4-5] #• ATARI 9-PIN* — Paddle inputs (A, B on pins 5, 6):
25124dfc [claude-haiku-4-5] #- These are typically RC timer inputs (like Apple II's `C064-C067`)
25124dfc [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Will need PIO state machines or interrupt-driven ADC timing to measure paddle resistance
25124dfc [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Button on pin 9 is straightforward digital input
25124dfd [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25124dfd [claude-haiku-4-5] #• VGA 15-PIN* — The DDC2B (I²C on ID pins) is interesting:
25124dfd [claude-haiku-4-5] #- GP0 (pin 12 SDA) and GP1 (pin 15 SCL) means your display detection shares pins with PS/2
25124dfe [claude-haiku-4-5] #- This could create contention if both are active — worth documenting which mode is primary
25124dfe [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25124dfe [claude-haiku-4-5] #• 74165 (Parallel-In Serial-Out)* — For keyboard matrix scanning?
25124dfe [claude-haiku-4-5] #- _LOAD (pin 1) and CLK (pin 2) would come from VIDBIT GPIOs
25124dfe [claude-haiku-4-5] #- 8-bit shift register feeds back via SER (pin 10) to capture key states
25124dff [claude-haiku-4-5] #- INH (pin 15) probably gates the clock during updates
25124dff [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25124dff [claude-haiku-4-5] #Questions
25124dff [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25124e00 [claude-haiku-4-5] #1. Pin Contention — Do PS/2 (GP0/GP1) and VGA DDC (GP0/GP1) modes switch dynamically, or is
25124e00 [claude-haiku-4-5] #one disabled?
25124e00 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25124e00 [claude-haiku-4-5] #2. Paddle Timing — How are you measuring paddle resistance? PIO-based timer or CPU-driven
25124e01 [claude-haiku-4-5] #polling?
25124e01 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25124e01 [claude-haiku-4-5] #3. 74165 Clock Rate — What frequency for the shift register? Typical keyboard scan is ~1–10
25124e01 [claude-haiku-4-5] #kHz.
25124e02 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25124e02 [claude-haiku-4-5] #4. Power Sequencing — VGA pin 9 is marked `* 5V KEY` — are you regulating from 5V input or
25124e02 [claude-haiku-4-5] #generating it locally?
25124e02 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25124e03 [claude-haiku-4-5] #The `simon was here` relay.md is nicely minimal. What's the current hardware status — prototype
25124e03 [claude-haiku-4-5] #stage or in testing?
25124e03 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
