2512512a [claude-haiku-4-5] #PICOTOOL & ENTHEOGEN Notes
2512512a [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2512512a [claude-haiku-4-5] #PICOTOOL Architecture
2512512b [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2512512b [claude-haiku-4-5] #• Good separation of concerns:*
2512512b [claude-haiku-4-5] #- PAL timing reference is well-documented (64 µs lines, 625 line frame)
2512512b [claude-haiku-4-5] #- RP2040/RP2350 clock math is explicit (8 ns/cycle at 125 MHz)
2512512c [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Mode switching (memory dump, scope, addressables, log) via BOOTSEL is practical
2512512c [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2512512c [claude-haiku-4-5] #• Code observations:*
2512512c [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2512512d [claude-haiku-4-5] #The `picoTool()` main loop handles:
2512512d [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Watchdog + RTC initialization
2512512d [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Serial ports, display, GPIO (buttons A/B), ADC, audio (SPDIF, speakers)
2512512d [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Button debouncing via `Button` class
2512512e [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Four application modes with clean switch structure
2512512e [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2512512e [claude-haiku-4-5] #• Potential issues:*
2512512e [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2512512f [claude-haiku-4-5] #1. Blocking `pollStdIn()` / `popCommandQueue()` — In a tight loop with `sleep_us(50)` (48
2512512f [claude-haiku-4-5] #kHz), these could add jitter to video timing. Consider interrupt-driven serial or buffered I/O.
2512512f [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2512512f [claude-haiku-4-5] #2. RGB LED mode (case 2) — Random rectangle fills + `rnd8()` every frame will flicker badly
25125130 [claude-haiku-4-5] #on a 240×135 display. Probably intentional for testing, but worth noting.
25125130 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25125130 [claude-haiku-4-5] #3. Memory dump mask logic — The `memmode` toggle between ROM and SRAM is clear, but
25125130 [claude-haiku-4-5] #`address=(address&0xfffffff&mask)|PICO_ROM` assumes `PICO_ROM` and `PICO_SRAM` are high-bit flags.
25125131 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Document those constants.
25125131 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25125131 [claude-haiku-4-5] #4. ADC init without selecting channel loop — `adc_select_input(0)` happens once, but if
25125131 [claude-haiku-4-5] #modes or later code switch channels, there's no re-selection in the main loop.
25125132 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25125132 [claude-haiku-4-5] #ENTHEOGEN / VIDBIT Integration
25125132 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25125132 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• USB VID Assignment:*
25125133 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- `0xF055` is custom (nitrologic's space)
25125133 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- `0x9801` = MicroPython
25125133 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- `0x9802` = VIDBIT
25125133 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25125133 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• SysEx structure* — Standard MIDI format, good for device control. One note:
25125134 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Manufacturer ID placeholder `0xXX` should be documented
25125134 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- If using custom ID space, ensure it doesn't conflict with existing MIDI vendors (check MIDI
25125134 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Manufacturers Association registry)
25125134 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25125135 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Questions
25125135 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25125135 [claude-haiku-4-5] #1. PAL video output — Are you generating composite video, component (YPbPr), or RGB/SCART?
25125135 [claude-haiku-4-5] #The 4.7 µs sync pulse timing suggests you're targeting real PAL spec compliance.
25125136 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25125136 [claude-haiku-4-5] #2. Button debounce duration — The `Button` class tracks state but I don't see hysteresis
25125136 [claude-haiku-4-5] #delay. How many frames before a press registers?
25125136 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25125137 [claude-haiku-4-5] #3. Display refresh — At 240×135 with `Rect()` draws per frame, what's the actual frame
25125137 [claude-haiku-4-5] #rate? Is it locked to PAL field rate (50 Hz) or free-running?
25125137 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25125137 [claude-haiku-4-5] #4. Dual-core usage — RP2350 has two cores. Is core 1 used for audio/video timing while core
25125138 [claude-haiku-4-5] #0 handles UI/commands?
25125138 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25125138 [claude-haiku-4-5] #The tooling is pragmatic. What's the current test status — booting games yet?
25125138 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
