25190994 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25190994 [claude-haiku-4-5] #I've reviewed the shared files:
25190994 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25190994 [claude-haiku-4-5] #1. relay.md - Project header (vintage CPU machines)
25190995 [claude-haiku-4-5] #2. machine.ts - Comprehensive 6502 emulator with multi-platform support (Apple II,
25190995 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Commodore 64, Plus/4, VIC-20, Atari, 1541 disk)
25190995 [claude-haiku-4-5] #3. notes.txt - TED (Plus/4) register initialization trace
25190995 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25190996 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Key Architecture Points
25190996 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25190996 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• Machine Class* is the core CPU emulator with:
25190996 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Full 6502 instruction set (180+ opcodes implemented)
25190997 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Platform-specific I/O handlers (readAddress/writeAddress dispatch)
25190997 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Cycle-accurate timing
25190997 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Interrupt handling (IRQ, NMI, BRK)
25190997 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Display rendering (text, graphics, vector)
25190997 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25190998 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• Multi-Machine Support*: Instances tracked in `machines` record, each with own
25190998 [claude-haiku-4-5] #memory/state, allowing simultaneous platforms.
25190998 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25190998 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• Platform Detection*: Flags like `isApple`, `isC64`, `isTED` control conditional I/O
25190999 [claude-haiku-4-5] #routing and display rendering.
25190999 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25190999 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Observations
25190999 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
2519099a [claude-haiku-4-5] #1. TED Support Incomplete - notes.txt shows register initialization but several
2519099a [claude-haiku-4-5] #`readTED`/`writeTED` handlers are stubs or log-only
2519099a [claude-haiku-4-5] #2. Display Rendering - Uses ANSI/Unicode for terminal output (braille, box chars, wide
2519099a [claude-haiku-4-5] #chars for 40-column CBM systems)
2519099b [claude-haiku-4-5] #3. Tape Simulation - CassetteRecorder handles WAV import/export with cycle-delta encoding
2519099b [claude-haiku-4-5] #4. DMA/Vector Engine - VectorEngine class present but minimal implementation (Atari Lunar
2519099b [claude-haiku-4-5] #Lander support)
2519099b [claude-haiku-4-5] #
