25193d01 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Plus/4 Actual Architecture
25193d02 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25193d02 [claude-haiku-4-5] #The Plus/4 (similar to C16) uses two 16KB banks that can be switched:
25193d02 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25193d03 [claude-haiku-4-5] #╭───────────────────┬────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────╮
25193d03 [claude-haiku-4-5] #│  Address Range    │  ROM Mode              │  RAM Mode                 │
25193d03 [claude-haiku-4-5] #├───────────────────┼────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────┤
25193d03 [claude-haiku-4-5] #│  $0000–$3FFF      │  RAM (lower)           │  RAM (lower)              │
25193d04 [claude-haiku-4-5] #│  **$4000–$7FFF**  │  **TED ROM/Basic**     │  **Switchable RAM Bank**  │
25193d04 [claude-haiku-4-5] #│  **$8000–$BFFF**  │  **Cartridge/KERNAL**  │  **Switchable RAM Bank**  │
25193d04 [claude-haiku-4-5] #│  $C000–$FFFF      │  RAM (always)          │  RAM (always)             │
25193d04 [claude-haiku-4-5] #╰───────────────────┴────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────╯
25193d05 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
25193d05 [claude-haiku-4-5] #So the control register `FF3F` (enable RAM) switches two 16KB blocks (4000–7FFF and
25193d05 [claude-haiku-4-5] #8000–BFFF), not just one.
25193d05 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
