253c2fd7 [claude-haiku-4-5] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 claude-haiku-4-5 A\ 🪠 🧊 $0.001 30.03KB 6.83s
253c2fd7 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Initial Assessment
253c2fd7 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c2fd7 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Reviewing the nitrologic arcade assembler project. This is a 6502 CPU assembler written in
253c2fd7 [claude-haiku-4-5] #TypeScript with Deno runtime.
253c2fd8 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c2fd8 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Observations
253c2fd8 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c2fd8 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• Structure is sound:*
253c2fd9 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Clean separation between instruction set (JSON) and parsing logic
253c2fd9 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Two-pass assembly approach for forward references
253c2fd9 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Mode enumeration covers 6502 addressing modes
253c2fd9 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Label and equate tracking with maps
253c2fda [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c2fda [claude-haiku-4-5] #• Current issues I notice:*
253c2fda [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c2fda [claude-haiku-4-5] #1. Incomplete addressing mode handling - The `parse6502()` function has several
253c2fdb [claude-haiku-4-5] #unimplemented cases in its switch statement, particularly for indexed and indirect modes. Only
253c2fdb [claude-haiku-4-5] #`Mode.Absolute` and `Mode.None` generate output.
253c2fdb [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c2fdc [claude-haiku-4-5] #2. Missing operand byte generation - When modes like `ZeroPageX`, `AbsoluteX`, etc. are
253c2fdc [claude-haiku-4-5] #detected, the code logs but doesn't emit the instruction bytes.
253c2fdc [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c2fdc [claude-haiku-4-5] #3. Opcode selection logic absent - For instructions with multiple opcodes (e.g., ADC has 8
253c2fdd [claude-haiku-4-5] #variants for different modes), there's no logic selecting the correct opcode byte from the
253c2fdd [claude-haiku-4-5] #instruction set's `opcodes` string.
253c2fdd [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c2fdd [claude-haiku-4-5] #4. Branch instruction offset calculation - Branch instructions (BCC, BEQ, etc.) need
253c2fde [claude-haiku-4-5] #relative offset computation, not addressed yet.
253c2fde [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c2fde [claude-haiku-4-5] #5. The `profile` array in JSON - Maps spec numbers to byte/cycle counts, but spec-to-mode
253c2fdf [claude-haiku-4-5] #mapping in assembly logic seems incomplete.
253c2fdf [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c2fdf [claude-haiku-4-5] #Are you starting with branch instruction support, or should we tackle the more fundamental opcode
253c2fdf [claude-haiku-4-5] #selection first?
253c2fe0 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
