253c3433 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Analysis of assembler.ts
253c3433 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c3433 [claude-haiku-4-5] #I've reviewed your 6502 assembler implementation. Here are the key observations:
253c3433 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c3433 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Current State
253c3433 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c3434 [claude-haiku-4-5] #The assembler is in active development with a solid foundation:
253c3434 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Label management: Working (setLabel, findLabel)
253c3434 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Equate handling: Implemented for byte/word references
253c3434 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Address modes: Partially implemented with parsing logic
253c3435 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Two-pass assembly: Framework in place
253c3435 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- JSON instruction set: Well-structured 6502 definition
253c3435 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c3435 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Issues Identified
253c3436 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c3436 [claude-haiku-4-5] #1. Incomplete Address Mode Coverage (notes.txt alert)
253c3436 [claude-haiku-4-5] #The `parse6502` function only handles:
253c3436 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- `Mode.Absolute` (fully)
253c3437 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- `Mode.None` (completely)
253c3437 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c3437 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Missing implementations for modes 0-10:
253c3437 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- `Immediate`, `Zeropage`, `ZeroPageX/Y`
253c3438 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- `AbsoluteX/Y`, `Indirect8/16`
253c3438 [claude-haiku-4-5] #- `Branch` mode
253c3438 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c3438 [claude-haiku-4-5] #2. Mode Detection Logic
253c3439 [claude-haiku-4-5] #The `addressMode` function parses modes correctly but `parse6502` doesn't generate bytecode for
253c3439 [claude-haiku-4-5] #most of them. The switch statement needs expansion.
253c3439 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c3439 [claude-haiku-4-5] #3. Byte Generation
253c343a [claude-haiku-4-5] #Currently returns placeholder `"00 00 00"` in `assemble6502()`. Real byte encoding needed based on:
253c343a [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Opcode from instruction set
253c343a [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Addressing mode from spec
253c343a [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Operand values
253c343a [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c343b [claude-haiku-4-5] #4. Label/Reference Resolution
253c343b [claude-haiku-4-5] #- `hex16()` has incomplete logic for resolving forward references
253c343b [claude-haiku-4-5] #- Two-pass assembly started but pass 2 doesn't rebuild bytecode
253c343b [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c343c [claude-haiku-4-5] #5. Memory Population
253c343c [claude-haiku-4-5] #The `ram` array is allocated but never populated with assembled bytes.
253c343c [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c343c [claude-haiku-4-5] #Recommended Next Steps
253c343d [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c343d [claude-haiku-4-5] #1. Complete the addressing mode switch in `parse6502()` with bytecode generation for all
253c343d [claude-haiku-4-5] #modes
253c343d [claude-haiku-4-5] #2. Implement byte encoding using instruction opcodes and operand values
253c343e [claude-haiku-4-5] #3. Fix two-pass assembly to rebuild bytecode on pass 2 after label resolution
253c343e [claude-haiku-4-5] #4. Populate ram with assembled instructions
253c343e [claude-haiku-4-5] #5. Add validation for unresolved forward references after pass 2
253c343e [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c343f [claude-haiku-4-5] #Would you like me to provide implementation details for any specific area?
253c343f [claude-haiku-4-5] #
