253c36dd [claude-haiku-4-5] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 claude-haiku-4-5 A\ 🪠 🧊 $0.002 32.65KB 5.78s
253c36dd [claude-haiku-4-5] #Spec 15 Analysis
253c36dd [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c36dd [claude-haiku-4-5] #You're absolutely right. Looking at the instruction set:
253c36dd [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c36de [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c36de [claude-haiku-4-5] #"ADC":{"opcodes":"69 65 75 6D 7D 79 61 71","flags":"NZCV","label":"ADD MEMORY TO ACCUMULATOR WITH CARRY","spec":15}
253c36de [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c36de [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c36df [claude-haiku-4-5] #• Spec 15* has 8 opcodes for 8 addressing modes. The `profile` array confirms this:
253c36df [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c36df [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c36df [claude-haiku-4-5] #{"bytes":[2,2,2,3,3,3,2,2],"cycles":[2,3,4,4,4,4,6,5]}
253c36e0 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c36e0 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c36e0 [claude-haiku-4-5] #That's the spec index mapping to:
253c36e0 [claude-haiku-4-5] #1. `69` - Immediate (#$xx) → 2 bytes
253c36e1 [claude-haiku-4-5] #2. `65` - Zeropage ($xx) → 2 bytes
253c36e1 [claude-haiku-4-5] #3. `75` - Zeropage,X ($xx,X) → 2 bytes
253c36e1 [claude-haiku-4-5] #4. `6D` - Absolute ($xxxx) → 3 bytes
253c36e1 [claude-haiku-4-5] #5. `7D` - Absolute,X ($xxxx,X) → 3 bytes
253c36e2 [claude-haiku-4-5] #6. `79` - Absolute,Y ($xxxx,Y) → 3 bytes
253c36e2 [claude-haiku-4-5] #7. `61` - (Indirect,X) ($xx,X) → 2 bytes
253c36e2 [claude-haiku-4-5] #8. `71` - (Indirect),Y ($xx),Y → 2 bytes
253c36e2 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c36e3 [claude-haiku-4-5] #The Fix
253c36e3 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c36e3 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Instead of a monolithic switch on `mode`, `parse6502` needs to:
253c36e4 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c36e4 [claude-haiku-4-5] #1. Map the detected `addressMode` to its index (0-7)
253c36e4 [claude-haiku-4-5] #2. Look up the correct opcode from `instruction.opcodes` using that index
253c36e4 [claude-haiku-4-5] #3. Encode the operand bytes based on the mode and profile
253c36e5 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c36e5 [claude-haiku-4-5] #The `spec` value is the key—it tells you which profile to use and implicitly which addressing modes
253c36e5 [claude-haiku-4-5] #are valid for that instruction.
253c36e5 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253c36e6 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Should I show a refactored approach for handling spec-based opcode selection?
