253cb94f [claude-haiku-4-5] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 claude-haiku-4-5 A\ 🪠 🧊 $0.002 23.15KB 6.43s
253cb94f [claude-haiku-4-5] #Thanks for sharing these files. I can see you're building a 6502 assembler for the nitrologic
253cb950 [claude-haiku-4-5] #arcade project.
253cb950 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253cb950 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Looking at the error in `notes.txt`, the issue is clear: Mode 1 (Immediate) isn't being handled
253cb950 [claude-haiku-4-5] #in the switch statement of the `parse6502` function around line 380.
253cb951 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253cb951 [claude-haiku-4-5] #The `addressMode` function correctly identifies immediate mode and returns `{mode: Mode.Immediate,
253cb951 [claude-haiku-4-5] #ref8: imm8}`, but the switch statement in `parse6502` only has cases for `Mode.Absolute` and
253cb951 [claude-haiku-4-5] #`Mode.None`, leaving immediate (and several other modes) unsupported.
253cb952 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253cb952 [claude-haiku-4-5] #The `AND` instruction with opcode `29` is the immediate variant (`AND #$xx`), which needs handling.
253cb952 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253cb952 [claude-haiku-4-5] #• Quick observations on the code:*
253cb953 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253cb953 [claude-haiku-4-5] #1. The `Mode` enum has syntax errors (`BAD` keywords shouldn't be there):
253cb953 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253cb953 [claude-haiku-4-5] #   enum Mode{
253cb954 [claude-haiku-4-5] #       ...
253cb954 [claude-haiku-4-5] #       BAD AbsoluteY,
253cb954 [claude-haiku-4-5] #       BAD Indirects,
253cb954 [claude-haiku-4-5] #       BAD IndirectX,
253cb955 [claude-haiku-4-5] #       ...
253cb955 [claude-haiku-4-5] #   }
253cb955 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253cb955 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253cb956 [claude-haiku-4-5] #2. Several mode cases reference types that don't exist in the enum (`Mode.Indirect8`,
253cb956 [claude-haiku-4-5] #`Mode.Indirect16`, etc.)
253cb956 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253cb956 [claude-haiku-4-5] #3. The switch in `parse6502` needs cases for `Mode.Immediate`, `Mode.Zeropage`, `Mode.ZeroPageX`,
253cb957 [claude-haiku-4-5] #`Mode.ZeroPageY`, `Mode.AbsoluteX`, `Mode.AbsoluteY`, and the indirect modes.
253cb957 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253cb957 [claude-haiku-4-5] #4. The `assemble6502` function hardcodes `"00 00 00"` for all hex bytes—it should actually emit the
253cb957 [claude-haiku-4-5] #generated bytes from `parse6502`.
253cb958 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
253cb958 [claude-haiku-4-5] #Would you like me to outline the fixes needed for the addressing mode handling?
253cb958 [claude-haiku-4-5] #
