25795809 [claude-sonnet-5] #When Chrome (or GitHub's markdown renderer, or VS Code's preview) displays that markdown file, it's
25795809 [claude-sonnet-5] #rendering actual Unicode codepoints for a given block — presumably Ethiopic or similar given the
25795809 [claude-sonnet-5] #`U+1300x` / `U+1301x` range labels — but wherever you're viewing it doesn't have a font installed
25795809 [claude-sonnet-5] #that covers those glyphs. So instead of the real character, you get the tofu/fallback `??` boxes.
2579580a [claude-sonnet-5] #
2579580a [claude-sonnet-5] #This is different from the translation-banner issue: that was Chrome's language detector
2579580a [claude-sonnet-5] #getting confused by the text content. This is a font coverage problem — the renderer knows
2579580a [claude-sonnet-5] #what codepoint to draw, it just has no glyph for it in any font available on that system, so it
2579580b [claude-sonnet-5] #substitutes a placeholder.
2579580b [claude-sonnet-5] #
2579580b [claude-sonnet-5] #A few things worth knowing:
2579580c [claude-sonnet-5] #
2579580c [claude-sonnet-5] #- `U+1300`–`U+137F` is the Ethiopic block — if that's what you're cataloguing, you'd need a
2579580c [claude-sonnet-5] #font like Noto Sans Ethiopic, Abyssinica SIL, or similar installed system-wide (or referenced via
2579580c [claude-sonnet-5] #`@font-face` if this is going through your `bibli.css`) for the glyphs to actually render.
2579580d [claude-sonnet-5] #- This is viewer-dependent, not data-dependent — the underlying codepoints in the `.md`
2579580d [claude-sonnet-5] #file are almost certainly correct; it's purely about whether the machine reading the file has the
2579580d [claude-sonnet-5] #right font. Same file could look perfect on one machine and be all `??` boxes on another.
2579580d [claude-sonnet-5] #- GitHub's own markdown renderer typically has broad Unicode font fallback baked in via web
2579580e [claude-sonnet-5] #fonts, so if this is `hieroglyph.md` or a similar block-listing file destined for GitHub Pages, it
2579580e [claude-sonnet-5] #might render fine there even if it looks broken locally in whatever editor/preview you're using.
