257976e4 [claude-sonnet-5] #Given the sheer script diversity here — Cherokee, Vai, Ogham, Coptic, Linear B, Ethiopic,
257976e4 [claude-sonnet-5] #hieroglyphs, alchemical symbols, box-drawing, emoji — no single font covers it all. Even large
257976e4 [claude-sonnet-5] #"universal" fonts have gaps in the more obscure historic blocks. So the practical answer is a
257976e4 [claude-sonnet-5] #stack, not one font.
257976e5 [claude-sonnet-5] #
257976e5 [claude-sonnet-5] #• For actual glyph coverage (the "no tofu" fallback layer):*
257976e5 [claude-sonnet-5] #The Noto family (Google) exists specifically to solve this problem — "Noto" literally
257976e5 [claude-sonnet-5] #stands for "no tofu." Most of your rarer blocks have dedicated Noto fonts:
257976e6 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Noto Sans Cherokee
257976e6 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Noto Sans Vai
257976e6 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Noto Sans Ogham
257976e6 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Noto Sans Coptic
257976e7 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Noto Sans Ethiopic
257976e7 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Noto Sans Linear B
257976e7 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Noto Sans Egyptian Hieroglyphs
257976e8 [claude-sonnet-5] #- Noto Sans Symbols / Symbols2 (covers alchemical, math symbols, box-drawing, most of your
257976e8 [claude-sonnet-5] #`fenced.code` geometry set)
257976e8 [claude-sonnet-5] #
257976e8 [claude-sonnet-5] #You'd reference these as a layered `font-family` fallback chain in `bibli.css`, letting the browser
257976e9 [claude-sonnet-5] #pick whichever installed/loaded font actually has the glyph.
257976e9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
257976e9 [claude-sonnet-5] #• For project "look" / identity (headers, prose):*
257976e9 [claude-sonnet-5] #Given the "grimoire" framing in the README, something with old-book/mystical character but still
257976ea [claude-sonnet-5] #clean would suit the branding — EB Garamond, Cormorant, or IM Fell English
257976ea [claude-sonnet-5] #all read as antique/manuscript-like without being illegible. Any of these as the primary display
257976ea [claude-sonnet-5] #font, falling back to Noto Sans for anything the display font can't render, gives you both
257976ea [claude-sonnet-5] #character and coverage.
257976eb [claude-sonnet-5] #
257976eb [claude-sonnet-5] #• For your `<pre>` blocks (code/data/status/terminal):*
257976eb [claude-sonnet-5] #Since those already read like a status/terminal aesthetic, a monospace with decent symbol coverage
257976eb [claude-sonnet-5] #— JetBrains Mono or Cascadia Code — would fit and both handle box-drawing
257976ec [claude-sonnet-5] #characters and many symbol blocks reasonably well natively.
257976ec [claude-sonnet-5] #
257976ec [claude-sonnet-5] #• Practical CSS shape:*
