2579840b [claude-sonnet-5] #A few notes on the choices:
2579840b [claude-sonnet-5] #
2579840c [claude-sonnet-5] #- `padding` — right now `margin` gives space outside the block, but there's nothing pushing
2579840c [claude-sonnet-5] #the text away from its own edges, so it can feel cramped against a background or border.
2579840c [claude-sonnet-5] #- `background-color` — a very light grey lifts it off the page as a distinct "block"
2579840c [claude-sonnet-5] #without shouting. If the rest of the page is on a dark theme, this would need inverting (something
2579840d [claude-sonnet-5] #like `#1e1e1e` background with lighter text).
2579840d [claude-sonnet-5] #- `border-left` — a thin accent border is a common "this is code/data" visual cue, subtler
2579840d [claude-sonnet-5] #than a full border box.
2579840d [claude-sonnet-5] #- `line-height` — `<pre>` content defaults to fairly tight line spacing; a touch more
2579840e [claude-sonnet-5] #breathing room helps readability at `x-large` size, especially with dense Unicode rows.
2579840e [claude-sonnet-5] #- `overflow-x: auto` — given some of your fullwidth/CJK/emoji rows can get quite long, this
2579840e [claude-sonnet-5] #prevents the block from blowing out page width and instead gives a horizontal scrollbar only when
2579840e [claude-sonnet-5] #needed.
