257990b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #CSS custom properties don't have any concept of "inherit the variable name from my own id."
257990b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #`var(--code-bg)` is just a static reference — the string `code-bg` isn't computed from the
257990b5 [claude-sonnet-5] #element's `id`, it's literally typed by you (or me) in the stylesheet. CSS has no templating or
257990b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #string-interpolation mechanism to do something like `var(--#{id}-bg)`. That's not a CSS limitation
257990b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #I'm working around badly — it genuinely doesn't exist in the language.
257990b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #
257990b6 [claude-sonnet-5] #So there are really only two honest options:
257990b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #
257990b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #• Option A — one shared variable, same background everywhere:*
257990b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #
257990b7 [claude-sonnet-5] #:root{
257990b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #	--pre-bg: #f6f6f6;
257990b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #}
257990b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #pre{
257990b8 [claude-sonnet-5] #	background-color: var(--pre-bg);
257990b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #}
257990b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
257990b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #Every `<pre>` gets the same background from one source of truth. Simple, but not "per-id."
257990b9 [claude-sonnet-5] #
257990ba [claude-sonnet-5] #• Option B — explicit per-id variables, no magic, but organised:*
257990ba [claude-sonnet-5] #
257990ba [claude-sonnet-5] #:root{
257990ba [claude-sonnet-5] #	--code-bg: #f6f6f6;
257990bb [claude-sonnet-5] #	--status-bg: #eef;
257990bb [claude-sonnet-5] #	--terminal-bg: #1e1e1e;
257990bb [claude-sonnet-5] #}
257990bb [claude-sonnet-5] ##code{ background-color: var(--code-bg); }
257990bc [claude-sonnet-5] ##status{ background-color: var(--status-bg); }
257990bc [claude-sonnet-5] ##terminal{ background-color: var(--terminal-bg); }
257990bc [claude-sonnet-5] #
257990bc [claude-sonnet-5] #Each block gets its own colour, but you have to name and wire each one manually — CSS can't infer
257990bd [claude-sonnet-5] #`--code-bg` from `id="code"` on its own.
257990bd [claude-sonnet-5] #
257990bd [claude-sonnet-5] #• If you actually want true "automatic per-id" behaviour* (e.g. every new `<pre
257990bd [claude-sonnet-5] #id="whatever">` magically gets its own colour without you touching the CSS again), that requires
257990be [claude-sonnet-5] #JavaScript — something like reading the element's `id` at runtime and setting an inline custom
257990be [claude-sonnet-5] #property or generating a colour from a hash of the name. That's a real and fairly common technique
257990be [claude-sonnet-5] #(deterministic colour-from-string, useful for tagging/avatars), but it lives in `bibli.js`, not in
257990bf [claude-sonnet-5] #the stylesheet.
257990bf [claude-sonnet-5] #
257990bf [claude-sonnet-5] #Which of these matches what you actually want — shared, manually-wired-per-block, or JS-generated?
257990bf [claude-sonnet-5] #
