25904019 [gemini-3.6-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.6-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.096 148.9KB 11.70s
25904019 [gemini-3.6-flash] #Here is an analysis of the reported issues based on the provided `machine.ts` source file:
2590401a [gemini-3.6-flash] #
2590401a [gemini-3.6-flash] #1. VIC-20 Keyboard Scanning Loop (`vic-20-2085.prg` stuck waiting for Space)
2590401a [gemini-3.6-flash] #• Root Cause: On hardware, VIC-20 keyboard scanning relies on VIA2 Port B (`9120`) to
2590401a [gemini-3.6-flash] #select columns and VIA1 Port A (`9111`) or VIA2 Port B (`$9121`) to read row responses.
2590401b [gemini-3.6-flash] #• Current Behavior:
2590401b [gemini-3.6-flash] #  * `readVIC` handles `9121` and `912F` by calling `readVIC20Matrix()`, but reading `$9111` returns
2590401b [gemini-3.6-flash] #a hardcoded joystick/tape variable (`via1porta`), completely bypassing the matrix state.
2590401b [gemini-3.6-flash] #  * In `tickVic()`, `9111` is populated using joystick and tape sense flags rather than evaluating
2590401c [gemini-3.6-flash] #active matrix lines selected by writes to `9120`.
2590401c [gemini-3.6-flash] #  * Because the Space key is part of the standard matrix matrix scan across VIA1 Port A / VIA2 Port
2590401c [gemini-3.6-flash] #B, routines polling `$9111` receive static values (`00` or `FF`) and loop indefinitely.
2590401c [gemini-3.6-flash] #
2590401d [gemini-3.6-flash] #2. VIC-20 3.5K Mode & Compatibility (Gridrunner)
2590401d [gemini-3.6-flash] #• Root Cause: An unexpanded VIC-20 locates BASIC RAM at `1000`–`1FFF` with Screen RAM
2590401d [gemini-3.6-flash] #located at `1E00`. Expanding memory (e.g., +8K or +16K) shifts user RAM start to `1200` and
2590401d [gemini-3.6-flash] #relocates Screen RAM to `1000`.
2590401e [gemini-3.6-flash] #• Current Behavior:
2590401e [gemini-3.6-flash] #  * `loadPRG` places program bytes into memory at the address defined by the file's two-byte origin
2590401e [gemini-3.6-flash] #header, but does not adjust BASIC pointer zero-page registers (`2B`–`2E`, `37`–`38`).
2590401e [gemini-3.6-flash] #  * If the emulator defaults to an expanded RAM map or fixed Screen RAM offsets, unexpanded PRG
2590401f [gemini-3.6-flash] #files like Gridrunner will fail to execute or will display corrupted video output due to mismatched
2590401f [gemini-3.6-flash] #screen and color memory addresses (`1E00`/`09600` vs `1000`/`09400`).
2590401f [gemini-3.6-flash] #
2590401f [gemini-3.6-flash] #3. VIC-20 Blink Speed
25904020 [gemini-3.6-flash] #• Root Cause: Flash/blink timing currently shares the global `frameCount` index derived
25904020 [gemini-3.6-flash] #from total CPU cycles divided by `62.5ms` ticks (`sixtieth`).
25904020 [gemini-3.6-flash] #• Current Behavior:
25904020 [gemini-3.6-flash] #  * In `displayAppleWide`, character blinking uses `frameCount & 64`, whereas Commodore video
25904021 [gemini-3.6-flash] #rendering passes through `displayPetScreenWide` on alternate frames (`frameCount & 1`).
25904021 [gemini-3.6-flash] #  * Because cycle counting and frame update intervals vary across platform configurations, the
25904021 [gemini-3.6-flash] #effective flash rate on the VIC-20 screen output runs faster than intended relative to Apple II
25904021 [gemini-3.6-flash] #character attribute toggling.
25904022 [gemini-3.6-flash] #
