25b91f3a [gemini-3.6-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.6-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.100 155.1KB 16.68s
25b91f3a [gemini-3.6-flash] #The provided code and log trace present two key components: a disassembly snippet from a Commodore
25b91f3a [gemini-3.6-flash] #PET 2001 ROM initialization sequence and a Deno/TypeScript 6502 emulator implementation
25b91f3b [gemini-3.6-flash] #(`machine.ts`).
25b91f3b [gemini-3.6-flash] #
25b91f3b [gemini-3.6-flash] #1. Analysis of the PET 2001 Startup Disassembly
25b91f3b [gemini-3.6-flash] #
25b91f3c [gemini-3.6-flash] #The disassembly sequence illustrates early hardware detection and state initialization on the MOS
25b91f3c [gemini-3.6-flash] #6502 processor and 6520/6522 peripheral ICs:
25b91f3c [gemini-3.6-flash] #
25b91f3c [gemini-3.6-flash] #• PIA1 Configuration (E810–E813):
25b91f3c [gemini-3.6-flash] #  * Reads `PIA1_PB` (`$E812`) and checks flags.
25b91f3d [gemini-3.6-flash] #  * Reads `PIA1_PA` (`E810`), masks high nibbles (`AND #F0`), and writes back `$00` to
25b91f3d [gemini-3.6-flash] #configure/clear line states.
25b91f3d [gemini-3.6-flash] #  * Writes `35` to `PIA1_CRB` (`E813`) to configure Control Register B (setting up CB2 control line
25b91f3d [gemini-3.6-flash] #behavior, typically managing the cassette motor or audio write line).
25b91f3e [gemini-3.6-flash] #• VIA Configuration ($E840):
25b91f3e [gemini-3.6-flash] #  * Reads `VIA_ORB` (`E840`), clears bit 4 (`AND #EF`), and writes back to disable or reset
25b91f3e [gemini-3.6-flash] #specific control signals.
25b91f3e [gemini-3.6-flash] #• Cassette & Timing Handshake Loop (E6F9–E75B):
25b91f3f [gemini-3.6-flash] #  * Polls `PIA1_PB` (`$E812`) to detect signal transitions.
25b91f3f [gemini-3.6-flash] #  * Shifts bit 0 (`LSR A` / `BCS`) to check line state before indexing into system timing tables
25b91f3f [gemini-3.6-flash] #located in ROM at `$E75B,X`.
25b91f3f [gemini-3.6-flash] #
25b91f40 [gemini-3.6-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
25b91f40 [gemini-3.6-flash] #
25b91f40 [gemini-3.6-flash] #2. Implementation Insights in `machine.ts`
25b91f41 [gemini-3.6-flash] #
25b91f41 [gemini-3.6-flash] #The emulator architecture cleanly models several retro hardware targets (PET, VIC-20, C64, Plus/4,
25b91f41 [gemini-3.6-flash] #Apple II, and Atari DVG systems). Key observation areas regarding PET and 6502 behavior include:
25b91f41 [gemini-3.6-flash] #
25b91f41 [gemini-3.6-flash] #• PIA1 Interrupt Line Clearing:
25b91f42 [gemini-3.6-flash] #  * In `readPET()`, reading `E812` explicitly masks bits 6 and 7 off in `E813` (`mem[0xE813] &=
25b91f42 [gemini-3.6-flash] #0x3f;`). This accurately reflects the hardware behavior of the 6520 PIA where reading Peripheral
25b91f42 [gemini-3.6-flash] #Register B clears active interrupt flags.
25b91f42 [gemini-3.6-flash] #• PETSCII and Display Matrix Mapping:
25b91f43 [gemini-3.6-flash] #  * Video memory is targeted at `$8000` (40×25 matrix). `displayPetScreenWide` maps memory bytes to
25b91f43 [gemini-3.6-flash] #double-width Unicode full-width characters (`petsciiUppercaseWide`), maintaining correct screen
25b91f43 [gemini-3.6-flash] #proportions in terminal environments.
25b91f43 [gemini-3.6-flash] #• Cassette Pulse Integration:
25b91f44 [gemini-3.6-flash] #  * `CassetteRecorder` measures transition deltas in CPU clock cycles (1.023\text MHz). The
25b91f44 [gemini-3.6-flash] #tristate level parser handles signal transitions, matching the timing expectations of PET ROM tape
25b91f44 [gemini-3.6-flash] #reading routines.
25b91f44 [gemini-3.6-flash] #
25b91f45 [gemini-3.6-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
25b91f45 [gemini-3.6-flash] #
25b91f45 [gemini-3.6-flash] #3. Key Points of Comparison & Considerations
25b91f46 [gemini-3.6-flash] #
25b91f46 [gemini-3.6-flash] #1. CB1 / CB2 Interrupt Signal Generation:
25b91f46 [gemini-3.6-flash] #   * In the disassembly trace at `E813`, bit 7 is expected to be toggled during frame cycles or
25b91f46 [gemini-3.6-flash] #cassette pulses. In `tick()`, bit 7 is set directly during vertical blanking (`mem[0xe813] |=
25b91f46 [gemini-3.6-flash] #0x80;`), satisfying the polling routine at `F77F`–`$F782`.
25b91f47 [gemini-3.6-flash] #2. Cycle Penalty Handling:
25b91f47 [gemini-3.6-flash] #   * Addressing routines like `readAbsoluteX`, `readAbsoluteY`, and `readIndirectY` account for the
25b91f47 [gemini-3.6-flash] #extra cycle incurred when crossing page boundaries (`(address ^ target) & 0xff00`).
25b91f47 [gemini-3.6-flash] #3. 6502 Page Boundary JMP Indirect Anomaly:
25b91f48 [gemini-3.6-flash] #   * The `JMP ($xxFF)` implementation explicitly models the hardware bug on the MOS 6502, wrapping
25b91f48 [gemini-3.6-flash] #the high byte fetch within the same page (`(pointer & 0xFF00) | ((pointer + 1) & 0x00FF)`).
25b91f48 [gemini-3.6-flash] #
25b91f49 [gemini-3.6-flash] #Please let me know if you would like me to modify or expand any specific subsystem or instruction
25b91f49 [gemini-3.6-flash] #handler within the source.
25b91f49 [gemini-3.6-flash] #
