25b9b7d4 [grok-build-0.1] #• Review of `z80.json`*
25b9b7d4 [grok-build-0.1] #
25b9b7d4 [grok-build-0.1] #This file is extremely minimal compared to your existing `mos6502.json` and `m6800.json`
25b9b7d4 [grok-build-0.1] #specifications.
25b9b7d5 [grok-build-0.1] #
25b9b7d5 [grok-build-0.1] #Current State
25b9b7d5 [grok-build-0.1] #
25b9b7d5 [grok-build-0.1] #
25b9b7d6 [grok-build-0.1] #{
25b9b7d6 [grok-build-0.1] #	"name": "Zilog Z80",
25b9b7d6 [grok-build-0.1] #	"description": "8 bit CPU",
25b9b7d6 [grok-build-0.1] #	"version": "0.0.1"
25b9b7d6 [grok-build-0.1] #}
25b9b7d7 [grok-build-0.1] #
25b9b7d7 [grok-build-0.1] #
25b9b7d7 [grok-build-0.1] #Gaps vs. Your Existing CPU Specs
25b9b7d7 [grok-build-0.1] #
25b9b7d8 [grok-build-0.1] #╭──────────────────────┬────────────────────────┬───────────────┬──────────────┬───────────────────────────────╮
25b9b7d8 [grok-build-0.1] #│  Field               │  6502 / 6800           │  Current Z80  │  Status      │  Notes                        │
25b9b7d8 [grok-build-0.1] #├──────────────────────┼────────────────────────┼───────────────┼──────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤
25b9b7d8 [grok-build-0.1] #│  `name`              │  Present               │  Present      │  OK          │  -                            │
25b9b7d8 [grok-build-0.1] #│  `description`       │  Present               │  Present      │  OK          │  -                            │
25b9b7d9 [grok-build-0.1] #│  `version`           │  Present               │  Present      │  OK          │  Very early                   │
25b9b7d9 [grok-build-0.1] #│  `copyright`         │  Present               │  Missing      │  Gap         │  Present in both other files  │
25b9b7d9 [grok-build-0.1] #│  `license`           │  Present               │  Missing      │  Gap         │  -                            │
25b9b7da [grok-build-0.1] #│  `repository`        │  Present               │  Missing      │  Gap         │  -                            │
25b9b7da [grok-build-0.1] #│  `addressmode`       │  Present               │  Missing      │  Major Gap   │  Z80 has many more modes      │
25b9b7da [grok-build-0.1] #│  `flags`             │  Present               │  Missing      │  Major Gap   │  -                            │
25b9b7da [grok-build-0.1] #│  `flagNames`         │  Present               │  Missing      │  Major Gap   │  -                            │
25b9b7db [grok-build-0.1] #│  `instruction`       │  Present (detailed)    │  Missing      │  Critical    │  This will be large           │
25b9b7db [grok-build-0.1] #│  `specprofile`       │  Present               │  Missing      │  Critical    │  Needed for timing            │
25b9b7db [grok-build-0.1] #│  `interrupts`        │  Present               │  Missing      │  Gap         │  -                            │
25b9b7db [grok-build-0.1] #╰──────────────────────┴────────────────────────┴───────────────┴──────────────┴───────────────────────────────╯
25b9b7db [grok-build-0.1] #
25b9b7dc [grok-build-0.1] #Key Observations
25b9b7dc [grok-build-0.1] #
25b9b7dc [grok-build-0.1] #- The Z80 has significantly more complexity than the 6502 or 6800. A full instruction set
25b9b7dc [grok-build-0.1] #will need to handle:
25b9b7dd [grok-build-0.1] #  - Unprefixed instructions
25b9b7dd [grok-build-0.1] #  - `CB` prefix (bit operations)
25b9b7dd [grok-build-0.1] #  - `DD` / `FD` prefixes (IX / IY indexed)
25b9b7dd [grok-build-0.1] #  - `ED` prefix (extended instructions)
25b9b7dd [grok-build-0.1] #  - Many instructions with multiple opcode lengths (1–4 bytes)
25b9b7de [grok-build-0.1] #
25b9b7de [grok-build-0.1] #- Your current 6502/6800 model uses a `"spec"` index into `specprofile` for byte/cycle counts. This
25b9b7de [grok-build-0.1] #approach will be much harder to apply cleanly to the Z80 because of the large number of
25b9b7de [grok-build-0.1] #timing variations and undocumented behaviors.
25b9b7df [grok-build-0.1] #
25b9b7df [grok-build-0.1] #- Z80 flags are different (`S`, `Z`, `H`, `P/V`, `N`, `C`). You'll need to decide how to represent
25b9b7df [grok-build-0.1] #the `P/V` flag (it serves as both Parity and Overflow).
25b9b7df [grok-build-0.1] #
25b9b7df [grok-build-0.1] #Recommendation
25b9b7e0 [grok-build-0.1] #
25b9b7e0 [grok-build-0.1] #If you want to keep consistency with your existing specs, the next logical steps would be to add:
25b9b7e0 [grok-build-0.1] #
25b9b7e0 [grok-build-0.1] #1. Header fields (`copyright`, `license`, `repository`)
25b9b7e0 [grok-build-0.1] #2. `flags` + `flagNames`
25b9b7e0 [grok-build-0.1] #3. `addressmode` array (Z80 has quite a few)
25b9b7e1 [grok-build-0.1] #4. A basic `instruction` skeleton
25b9b7e1 [grok-build-0.1] #
25b9b7e1 [grok-build-0.1] #Would you like me to:
25b9b7e1 [grok-build-0.1] #
25b9b7e1 [grok-build-0.1] #- Give you a recommended base structure for `z80.json` that matches the style of your
25b9b7e2 [grok-build-0.1] #6502/6800 files?
25b9b7e2 [grok-build-0.1] #- Or focus on just the `addressmode` and `flags` sections first?
25b9b7e2 [grok-build-0.1] #
25b9b7e2 [grok-build-0.1] #Let me know how you want to proceed.
25b9b7e2 [grok-build-0.1] #
