25b9e857 [grok-build-0.1] #"RLA",:{},
25b9e857 [grok-build-0.1] #
25b9e857 [grok-build-0.1] #
25b9e858 [grok-build-0.1] #That is invalid JSON. After a string key in an object, the parser expects a colon (`:`), not a
25b9e858 [grok-build-0.1] #comma. I treated it too casually as a minor formatting issue. That was a mistake on my part.
25b9e858 [grok-build-0.1] #
25b9e858 [grok-build-0.1] #The current file you just posted does not contain that error (or any other obvious trailing/syntax
