25f7eb78 [glm-5.2] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 glm-5.2 Z 🪠 0.7° $0.017 26.23KB 15.43s
25f7eb79 [glm-5.2] #Apologies for any confusion. There is no issue at all with opcodes `89` through `8F` in your
25f7eb79 [glm-5.2] #`encoding` block—they are perfectly accurate there.
25f7eb79 [glm-5.2] #
25f7eb79 [glm-5.2] #My comment was specifically regarding the `forms` array inside the `instruction` object for `ADC`:
25f7eb7a [glm-5.2] #
25f7eb7a [glm-5.2] #`"forms": ["CE","88","ED 4A","8E","DD 8E","FD 8E"]`
25f7eb7a [glm-5.2] #
25f7eb7a [glm-5.2] #In that array, you included `"88"` (ADC A,B) and `"8E"` (ADC A,(HL)), but the other 8-bit register
25f7eb7b [glm-5.2] #variants (`89` ADC A,C, `8A` ADC A,D, `8B` ADC A,E, `8C` ADC A,H, `8D` ADC A,L, and `8F` ADC A,A)
25f7eb7b [glm-5.2] #were not listed.
25f7eb7b [glm-5.2] #
25f7eb7b [glm-5.2] #If your engine or assembler relies on that `forms` array to look up valid opcodes for the `ADC`
25f7eb7c [glm-5.2] #instruction, it would miss those specific register combinations.
