25f80c2e [glm-5.2] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 glm-5.2 Z 🪠 0.7° $0.019 37.99KB 7.44s
25f80c2e [glm-5.2] #Yes, that covers all of the officially documented forms of the `ADC` instruction for the Z80.
25f80c2e [glm-5.2] #
25f80c2e [glm-5.2] #To summarize, you have:
25f80c2e [glm-5.2] #• `ADC A, r` (8-bit register to accumulator)
25f80c2f [glm-5.2] #• `ADC A, (HL)` (8-bit memory to accumulator)
25f80c2f [glm-5.2] #• `ADC A, n` (8-bit immediate to accumulator)
25f80c2f [glm-5.2] #• `ADC A, (IX+d)` / `ADC A, (IY+d)` (8-bit indexed memory to accumulator)
25f80c2f [glm-5.2] #• `ADC HL, rr` (16-bit register to HL)
25f80c30 [glm-5.2] #
25f80c30 [glm-5.2] #The only thing not included here are the undocumented `ADC A, IXH`/`IXL`/`IYH`/`IYL` variations
25f80c30 [glm-5.2] #(often referred to as the `H` and `L` halves of the index registers). If you are strictly sticking
25f80c31 [glm-5.2] #to the documented Z80 specification, your list is complete.
25f80c31 [glm-5.2] #
