25f96ede [nitro@ryzen5] how many registers does z80 have?
25f96fb2 [glm-5.2] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 glm-5.2 Z 🪠 0.7° $0.007 570B 12.86s
25f96fb2 [glm-5.2] #Hello. The Zilog Z80 microprocessor has a total of 22 registers. They are generally categorized as
25f96fb2 [glm-5.2] #follows:
25f96fb3 [glm-5.2] #
25f96fb3 [glm-5.2] #• Main Registers (8): A, F, B, C, D, E, H, and L. These are 8-bit registers, though they
25f96fb3 [glm-5.2] #can be paired up (AF, BC, DE, HL) to perform 16-bit operations.
25f96fb3 [glm-5.2] #• Shadow Registers (8): A', F', B', C', D', E', H', and L'. These are alternate versions of
25f96fb4 [glm-5.2] #the main registers. They cannot be addressed directly, but contents can be exchanged with the main
25f96fb4 [glm-5.2] #registers using specific instructions, which is useful for fast context switching during
25f96fb4 [glm-5.2] #interrupts.
25f96fb4 [glm-5.2] #• Index Registers (2): IX and IY. These are 16-bit registers used primarily for indexed
25f96fb5 [glm-5.2] #addressing modes.
25f96fb5 [glm-5.2] #• System Registers (2): PC (Program Counter) and SP (Stack Pointer). These are 16-bit
25f96fb5 [glm-5.2] #registers used to manage execution flow and the stack memory.
25f96fb5 [glm-5.2] #• Special Purpose Registers (2): I (Interrupt Vector) and R (Memory Refresh Counter). These
25f96fb6 [glm-5.2] #are 8-bit registers used for interrupt handling and dynamic RAM refreshing, respectively.
25f96fb6 [glm-5.2] #
25f96fb6 [glm-5.2] #Please let me know if you would like more detailed information on any of these.
25f96fb6 [glm-5.2] #
