260e017e [gemini-3.7-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.003 841B 4.13s
260e017e [gemini-3.7-flash] #Yes, using a custom font in both Windows and macOS terminals is straightforward and generally
260e017e [gemini-3.7-flash] #involves two main steps: installing the font onto your system, and then selecting it in your
260e017e [gemini-3.7-flash] #terminal's settings.
260e017e [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260e017e [gemini-3.7-flash] #Here is a brief overview of how the process works on each platform:
260e017f [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260e017f [gemini-3.7-flash] #macOS (Terminal.app or iTerm2)
260e017f [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. Install the font: Download your desired font file (`.ttf` or `.otf`) and open it with
260e017f [gemini-3.7-flash] #Font Book, then click Install Font.
260e017f [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. Apply the font:
260e017f [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * In Terminal, open Settings (or Preferences) \rightarrow
260e0180 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Profiles \rightarrow Text, click the Change button under the Font section,
260e0180 [gemini-3.7-flash] #and choose your installed font.
260e0180 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * In iTerm2, navigate to Settings \rightarrow Profiles \rightarrow
260e0180 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Text and select the font from the drop-down menu.
260e0181 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260e0181 [gemini-3.7-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
260e0181 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260e0181 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Windows (Windows Terminal)
260e0182 [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. Install the font: Right-click the downloaded font file (`.ttf` or `.otf`) and choose
260e0182 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Install or Install for all users.
260e0182 [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. Apply the font:
260e0182 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * Open Windows Terminal, open Settings, and select your default profile (or a
260e0182 [gemini-3.7-flash] #specific profile like PowerShell or Command Prompt).
260e0183 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * Go to Appearance, and select your font from the Font face drop-down list.
260e0183 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260e0183 [gemini-3.7-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
260e0183 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260e0184 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Key Consideration
260e0184 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Terminals generally require or strongly prefer monospaced fonts (such as Fira
260e0184 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Code, JetBrains Mono, or Cascadia Code). While some terminals allow
260e0184 [gemini-3.7-flash] #proportional fonts, monospaced fonts ensure that columns, tables, and command line tools align
260e0184 [gemini-3.7-flash] #correctly.
260e0185 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260e0185 [gemini-3.7-flash] #If you would like detailed, step-by-step guidance for a specific terminal application or font type
260e0185 [gemini-3.7-flash] #(such as Nerd Fonts with glyph support), please let me know.
260e0185 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
