260e964e [nitro@ryzen5] on vic20 is runstop key special?
260e96b3 [gemini-3.7-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.004 497B 5.82s
260e96b3 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Yes, the RUN/STOP key is quite special on the Commodore VIC-20, serving as a primary
260e96b3 [gemini-3.7-flash] #control key for both the operating system (KERNAL) and BASIC environment.
260e96b3 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260e96b3 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Here are the main ways it functions:
260e96b3 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260e96b3 [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. Halting Program Execution
260e96b3 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Pressed on its own while a BASIC program is executing, it immediately interrupts the program and
260e96b4 [gemini-3.7-flash] #returns control to the user, displaying a `BREAK IN LINE [X]` message.
260e96b4 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260e96b4 [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. Auto-Loading from Tape (`SHIFT` + `RUN/STOP`)
260e96b4 [gemini-3.7-flash] #When pressed in combination with the SHIFT key, it acts as a shortcut to load and run the
260e96b4 [gemini-3.7-flash] #next program from a connected Commodore Datassette tape drive. It automatically prints `LOAD` to
260e96b4 [gemini-3.7-flash] #the screen, prompts the user to press PLAY on the tape unit, and automatically executes `RUN` once
260e96b5 [gemini-3.7-flash] #loading finishes.
260e96b5 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260e96b5 [gemini-3.7-flash] #3. Warm Reset (`RUN/STOP` + `RESTORE`)
260e96b5 [gemini-3.7-flash] #When held down while pressing the RESTORE key, it triggers a Non-Maskable Interrupt (NMI)
260e96b6 [gemini-3.7-flash] #on the 6502 processor. This performs a "warm reset," which:
260e96b6 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Clears the screen and resets text colors to default.
260e96b6 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Silences the sound registers.
260e96b6 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Returns the system to the `READY.` prompt while preserving the BASIC program currently in
260e96b6 [gemini-3.7-flash] #memory.
260e96b7 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260e96b7 [gemini-3.7-flash] #4. Software Control and Trapping
260e96b7 [gemini-3.7-flash] #From a programming perspective, the KERNAL actively polls the keyboard matrix specifically looking
260e96b7 [gemini-3.7-flash] #for the RUN/STOP key during execution. Programmers can disable or repurpose the key by modifying
260e96b8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #system vectors in memory (such as redirecting the break or NMI vectors) to prevent users from
260e96b8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #stopping commercial software or games.
260e96b8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
