260ea40c [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260ea40c [gemini-3.7-flash] #Context Note
260ea40d [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Standard keyboard messages (such as `WM_KEYDOWN` or `WM_KEYUP`) generally report the generic
260ea40d [gemini-3.7-flash] #`VK_SHIFT` (`0x10` / `16`).
260ea40d [gemini-3.7-flash] #• The distinct `VK_LSHIFT` and `VK_RSHIFT` codes are typically used with functions that poll the
260ea40d [gemini-3.7-flash] #specific physical key state, such as `GetAsyncKeyState()` or `GetKeyState()`, or when processing
