260ef046 [gemini-3.7-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.003 12.42KB 1.89s
260ef046 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• No, the Control key does not change the Virtual-Key (VK) codes of other keys.*
260ef046 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260ef046 [gemini-3.7-flash] #In the Windows input model:
260ef047 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260ef047 [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. VK Codes are Physical Identifiers:
260ef047 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   When you press `Ctrl + C`, the system emits two distinct events:
260ef047 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * Event 1: `VK_CONTROL` (`0x11`) or `VK_LCONTROL` (`0xA2`)
260ef048 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * Event 2: `0x43` (VK code for `'C'`)
260ef048 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   The VK code for `'C'` remains `0x43` regardless of whether Control, Shift, or Alt is held down.
260ef048 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260ef048 [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. Character Codes (ASCII) Do Change:
260ef049 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   While the VK code stays the same, the resulting character translation (e.g., `WM_CHAR`
260ef049 [gemini-3.7-flash] #or text input) changes into non-printable ASCII control characters:
260ef049 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * Pressing `'A'` generates character code `65` (`'A'`) or `97` (`'a'`).
260ef049 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * Pressing `Ctrl + A` generates character code `1` (`0x01`, SOH).
260ef049 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * Pressing `Ctrl + C` generates character code `3` (`0x03`, ETX).
260ef049 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260ef04a [gemini-3.7-flash] #Summary for Keyboard Emulation:
260ef04a [gemini-3.7-flash] #If you are matching host key presses to your VIC-20 keyboard matrix using VK codes
260ef04a [gemini-3.7-flash] #(`keydown` / `WM_KEYDOWN`), modifier keys like `Ctrl` will not alter the codes received for other
260ef04a [gemini-3.7-flash] #keys.
260ef04a [gemini-3.7-flash] #
