260ef866 [gemini-3.7-flash] #There are two main reasons why `0xA0` (Left Shift), `0xA1` (Right Shift), and
260ef866 [gemini-3.7-flash] #`0xA2` (Commodore key) are not working as expected:
260ef866 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260ef866 [gemini-3.7-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
260ef867 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260ef867 [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. Matrix Wiring Row/Column Transposition
260ef867 [gemini-3.7-flash] #The standard VIC-20 hardware matrix (VIA #1 Port B / VIA #2 Port A) places modifier keys in
260ef867 [gemini-3.7-flash] #specific slots:
260ef868 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260ef868 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Left Shift is located at Row 4, Column 1 in the matrix (wired alongside `Z, C, B,
260ef868 [gemini-3.7-flash] #M, .`). In your current array, it is placed in Row 3 with `X, V, N`.
260ef869 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Right Shift is located at Row 3, Column 6 (wired alongside `X, V, N, ,, /`). In
260ef869 [gemini-3.7-flash] #your current array, it is placed in Row 4 with `Z, C, B, M`.
260ef869 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Commodore Key (C=) is located at Row 5, Column 0 (wired alongside `S, F, H, K,
260ef869 [gemini-3.7-flash] #:`).
260ef86a [gemini-3.7-flash] #• RUN/STOP is located at Row 3, Column 0 (currently set to `0x00`).
260ef86a [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260ef86a [gemini-3.7-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
260ef86a [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260ef86b [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. Physical Placement of Modifiers on Host Keyboards
260ef86b [gemini-3.7-flash] #When emulating a Commodore machine on a modern PC keyboard, using `0xA2` (Left Control) for
260ef86b [gemini-3.7-flash] #the Commodore Key creates a conflict if you also want to use the VIC-20's `CTRL` key.
260ef86b [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260ef86c [gemini-3.7-flash] #Common PC mappings:
260ef86c [gemini-3.7-flash] #• VIC-20 `CTRL` Key \rightarrow mapped to Left Ctrl (`0xA2`) or generic
260ef86c [gemini-3.7-flash] #`VK_CONTROL` (`0x11`) at Row 2, Column 0 (currently `0x70` / F1).
260ef86d [gemini-3.7-flash] #• VIC-20 `C=` Key \rightarrow mapped to Left Alt / Menu (`0xA4` / `VK_LMENU`) or
260ef86d [gemini-3.7-flash] #Left Windows (`0x5B` / `VK_LWIN`) at Row 5, Column 0.
260ef86d [gemini-3.7-flash] #• VIC-20 `RUN/STOP` Key \rightarrow mapped to ESC (`0x1B`) or Pause/Break
260ef86d [gemini-3.7-flash] #(`0x13`) at Row 3, Column 0.
260ef86e [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260ef86e [gemini-3.7-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
