260f9088 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Observations and Refinements
260f9088 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260f9088 [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. CCR Initialization
260f9088 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * The `ccr` property is declared as a `number` on the class, but it is currently not initialized
260f9088 [gemini-3.7-flash] #in the constructor.
260f9089 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * On hardware reset, the upper two bits (bits 6 and 7) are typically tied high (`0xC0`), and the
260f9089 [gemini-3.7-flash] #interrupt mask flag (`IFLAG` / `0x10`) is set to prevent interrupts before initialization. Setting
260f9089 [gemini-3.7-flash] #`this.ccr = 0xD0;` (bits 7, 6, and `I` set) in the constructor is standard practice for
260f9089 [gemini-3.7-flash] #power-on/reset.
260f908a [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260f908a [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. Register Array Indexing
260f908a [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * Defining explicit constant indices for `registers` (`PC`, `SP`, `X`) and `accumulators` (`A`,
260f908b [gemini-3.7-flash] #`B`) avoids magic numbers throughout the instruction execution methods:
260f908b [gemini-3.7-flash] #     * `const REG_PC = 0; const REG_SP = 1; const REG_X = 2;`
260f908b [gemini-3.7-flash] #     * `const ACC_A = 0; const ACC_B = 1;`
260f908b [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260f908c [gemini-3.7-flash] #3. Condition Flag Values
260f908c [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * The flag bitmasks (`CFLAG = 1` through `HFLAG = 32`) match the bit positions of the Motorola
260f908c [gemini-3.7-flash] #6800 CCR layout.
260f908c [gemini-3.7-flash] #
260f908d [gemini-3.7-flash] #Let me know if you would like helper functions defined for flag evaluation, addressing mode
260f908d [gemini-3.7-flash] #resolution, or instruction dispatch.
260f908d [gemini-3.7-flash] #
