26239b40 [gemini-3.7-flash] #This loop is the PET Editor ROM's `CHRIN` / `BASIN` line input wait loop.
26239b40 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
26239b40 [gemini-3.7-flash] #What the Code is Doing
26239b41 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
26239b41 [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. Wait State: Location `$020D` acts as the input line length / Return flag for the
26239b41 [gemini-3.7-flash] #screen editor.
26239b41 [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. The Loop: While `020D` is `0`, no completed line (terminated by the `RETURN` key) is
26239b42 [gemini-3.7-flash] #ready for BASIC to process. The routine continuously loops at `E297`, waiting for input.
26239b42 [gemini-3.7-flash] #3. Exit Condition: When the user types a command and presses `RETURN`, the editor updates
26239b42 [gemini-3.7-flash] #`020D` with the number of characters in the current logical screen line. The loop then branches
26239b42 [gemini-3.7-flash] #past `E29D` so BASIC can read and evaluate the input.
26239b43 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
26239b43 [gemini-3.7-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
26239b43 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
26239b43 [gemini-3.7-flash] #What This Means for Your Simulator
26239b44 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
26239b44 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• If the startup banner (` COMMODORE BASIC `, memory size, `READY.`) is visible
26239b44 [gemini-3.7-flash] #on the screen:
26239b44 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  Your simulator has successfully booted. The CPU is idling at the `READY.` prompt, waiting for
26239b45 [gemini-3.7-flash] #user keyboard input.
26239b45 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
26239b45 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• If the screen is still blank or no prompt appeared:
26239b45 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  1. Hardware IRQ Timer: Ensure your simulator is generating periodic interrupts (the ~60
26239b46 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Hz PIA 1 / VIA timer tick). The IRQ service routine is responsible for blinking the cursor and
26239b46 [gemini-3.7-flash] #scanning keyboard matrix lines.
26239b46 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  2. Keyboard Matrix Simulation: When simulating key presses, ensure the keyboard scan
26239b46 [gemini-3.7-flash] #routine receives the key matrix changes at `E810` / `E812` so it can populate the keyboard buffer.
26239b47 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
