262b9b1e [gemini-3.7-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.009 37.27KB 3.14s
262b9b1e [gemini-3.7-flash] #In the PET's screen character set (Screen Codes):
262b9b1e [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262b9b1f [gemini-3.7-flash] #• `$00` represents the `@` character.
262b9b1f [gemini-3.7-flash] #• `$20` represents a Space (` `).
262b9b1f [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262b9b1f [gemini-3.7-flash] #Screen Codes vs. PETSCII
262b9b20 [gemini-3.7-flash] #The Commodore PET does not store standard PETSCII/ASCII directly in video RAM (`8000–83E7`).
262b9b20 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Instead, the hardware character generator ROM is indexed using Screen Codes:
262b9b20 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262b9b20 [gemini-3.7-flash] #╭─────────────┬─────────────────────┬─────────────────╮
262b9b21 [gemini-3.7-flash] #│  Character  │  Screen Code (Hex)  │  PETSCII (Hex)  │
262b9b21 [gemini-3.7-flash] #├─────────────┼─────────────────────┼─────────────────┤
262b9b21 [gemini-3.7-flash] #│  :---       │  :---               │  :---           │
262b9b21 [gemini-3.7-flash] #│  **`@`**    │  **`$00`**          │  `$40`          │
262b9b22 [gemini-3.7-flash] #│  `A`        │  `$01`              │  `$41`          │
262b9b22 [gemini-3.7-flash] #│  `B`        │  `$02`              │  `$42`          │
262b9b22 [gemini-3.7-flash] #│  ...        │  ...                │  ...            │
262b9b22 [gemini-3.7-flash] #│  **Space**  │  **`$20`**          │  **`$20`**      │
262b9b23 [gemini-3.7-flash] #╰─────────────┴─────────────────────┴─────────────────╯
262b9b23 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262b9b23 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Because video RAM filled with `00` displays as a screen full of `@` symbols (often seen briefly on
262b9b23 [gemini-3.7-flash] #real hardware at power-up before the Kernal executes the screen-clear routine), the PET Kernal will
262b9b24 [gemini-3.7-flash] #soon write `20` to the entire 1000-byte video buffer to blank/clear the display before printing the
262b9b24 [gemini-3.7-flash] #startup banner.
262b9b24 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
