262bafd9 [gemini-3.7-flash] #This loop is the RAM sizing and destructive test routine (`RAMTAS`). It tests every byte
262bafda [gemini-3.7-flash] #from `0400` upward by writing `92`, reading it back, shifting it (`ASL`), writing `24`, and reading
262bafda [gemini-3.7-flash] #it back to find the upper limit of installed RAM (stopping before `8000` video RAM or when writes
262bafda [gemini-3.7-flash] #fail to read back).
262bafda [gemini-3.7-flash] #
