262bb870 [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. Carriage Return (`0D`) Screen Handler (`E3FF–$E556`)
262bb870 [gemini-3.7-flash] #The screen editor processes the `$0D` (Carriage Return) sent in the previous trace:
262bb870 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262bb871 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Cursor Reset (`E548–E551`):
262bb871 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * Sets `$E2 = 0` (moves the cursor to column 0, the start of the line).
262bb871 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * Clears quote mode (`FB = 0`) and insert mode (`020E = 0`).
262bb871 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262bb872 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Advance to Next Line (`E530–E545`):
262bb872 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * `LDX F5` / `INX`: Increments the current cursor row from `1` to `2` (`F5 = $02`).
262bb872 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * `CPX #19`: Checks if the bottom of the screen (line 25 / `19`) has been reached. Since it
262bb872 [gemini-3.7-flash] #hasn't, no upward screen scrolling is needed.
262bb873 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262bb873 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Recompute Video Row Pointer (`E5DB–E604`):
262bb873 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * Reads the row offset tables:
262bb873 [gemini-3.7-flash] #    * `E7BE` \rightarrow `50` (decimal 80 = 2 × 40 character offset).
262bb874 [gemini-3.7-flash] #    * High byte base \rightarrow `$80`.
262bb874 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * Stores `8050` into the screen pointer `E0/$E1` (row 2, column 0 of screen RAM).
262bb874 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262bb874 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Return to Caller (`E38A–E396`):
262bb875 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * Restores registers from the stack, enables interrupts (`CLI`), and returns from the CR handling
262bb875 [gemini-3.7-flash] #routine.
262bb875 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
