262bed08 [gemini-3.7-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.042 156.3KB 5.74s
262bed08 [gemini-3.7-flash] #On the Commodore PET, VIA PB5 (`$E840`, Bit 5) is connected specifically to the
262bed08 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Combined Video Blanking / Retrace signal coming from the discrete video timing logic (or
262bed08 [gemini-3.7-flash] #the CRTC in later models), but in terms of timing, it checks both horizontal and vertical
262bed08 [gemini-3.7-flash] #blanking:
262bed09 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262bed09 [gemini-3.7-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
262bed09 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262bed09 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Hardware Details
262bed0a [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262bed0a [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. The Circuit Connection:
262bed0a [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * On original dynamic-board PETs (e.g., 2001, 2001-N, 3032, early 4032s), the PET uses discrete
262bed0a [gemini-3.7-flash] #TTL counters (like 74LS163 / 74LS74) to generate video timing.
262bed0b [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * The hardware combines Horizontal Blanking (\sim16\text–20\ μ\texts per scanline) and
262bed0b [gemini-3.7-flash] #Vertical Blanking (\sim1.2\text–1.5\text ms per field) into a single master composite
262bed0b [gemini-3.7-flash] #`BLANK` (or `RETRACE`) line.
262bed0b [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * This master blanking line is tied to VIA Pin 15 (Port B, Bit 5).
262bed0c [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262bed0c [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. Why Horizontal Retrace is Critical for Single-Character Writes:
262bed0c [gemini-3.7-flash] #    Vertical blanking only happens 50/60 times per second (once every \sim16.6\text ms
262bed0c [gemini-3.7-flash] #or 20\text ms). If the Kernal waited for a vertical blank on every single character* printed,
262bed0d [gemini-3.7-flash] #printing a 40-character line would take almost a full second.
262bed0d [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * Instead, by syncing to the blanking line, the tight two-instruction loop (`LDA E840` / `AND
262bed0d [gemini-3.7-flash] ##20` / `BNE`) catches the next Horizontal Blanking interval (which occurs roughly every 64\
262bed0d [gemini-3.7-flash] #μ\texts).
262bed0e [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * As soon as the electron beam hits the right margin and turns off to travel back left, the CPU
262bed0e [gemini-3.7-flash] #writes the character to video RAM before the beam starts drawing the next scanline.
262bed0e [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262bed0e [gemini-3.7-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
262bed0f [gemini-3.7-flash] #
262bed0f [gemini-3.7-flash] #In Summary
262bed0f [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Interrupts (Timer / 60 Hz system clock): Synced to Vertical Sync (via PIA1 CB1 /
262bed0f [gemini-3.7-flash] #VIA CB2).
262bed10 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Character Screen Writes (`VIA_ORB` Bit 5 at `$E7AD`): Checks the composite
262bed10 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Blanking signal, which allows each individual character write to slip into the next
262bed10 [gemini-3.7-flash] #available Horizontal Retrace without stalling the CPU.
262bed10 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
