26383db4 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
26383db5 [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. Software-Written Bits (Bits 0–5)
26383db5 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Bits 0 through 5 are written directly by the CPU to configure the PIA's operating mode:
26383db5 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
26383db5 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Bit 0 (CA1 Interrupt Enable):
26383db6 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * `0`: Disables IRQ generation from the CA1 line.
26383db6 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * `1`: Enables IRQ generation to the 6502 when the CA1 interrupt condition occurs.
26383db6 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Bit 1 (CA1 Active Transition Select):
26383db7 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * `0`: Detects a high-to-low (falling edge) transition on CA1.
26383db7 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * `1`: Detects a low-to-high (rising edge) transition on CA1.
26383db7 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Bit 2 (Data Direction Register Access):
26383db7 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * `0`: Directs reads/writes at `$E810` to the Data Direction Register A (DDRA).
26383db7 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * `1`: Directs reads/writes at `$E810` to the Port A Output Register / Input Pins (PRA).
26383db7 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Bits 3, 4, and 5 (CA2 Control):
26383db8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * Configure the operation of the CA2 line (e.g., input interrupt mode, pulse output mode, or
26383db8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #fixed manual output level).
26383db8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
26383db8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
26383db9 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
26383db9 [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. Hardware-Driven Status Flags (Bits 6 & 7)
26383db9 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Bits 6 and 7 are read-only flags set directly by electrical transitions on the external control
26383db9 [gemini-3.7-flash] #pins:
26383dba [gemini-3.7-flash] #
26383dba [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Bit 6 (IRQA2 Flag):
26383dba [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * Set to `1` by an active transition on the CA2 line when configured as an input.
26383dba [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * On most PET mainboards, CA2 is commonly configured by the ROM as an output to control the
26383dbb [gemini-3.7-flash] #Cassette #1 Motor line, keeping this flag inactive during standard operation.
26383dbb [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Bit 7 (IRQA1 Flag):
26383dbb [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * Set to `1` when an active edge occurs on the CA1 line.
26383dbb [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * On the PET hardware, the CA1 line is physically connected to the Cassette #1 Read
26383dbc [gemini-3.7-flash] #Data line. Pulses coming from the tape read head toggle this flag.
26383dbc [gemini-3.7-flash] #
26383dbc [gemini-3.7-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
26383dbc [gemini-3.7-flash] #
26383dbd [gemini-3.7-flash] #3. Reset and Clearing Behavior
26383dbd [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Reset: A hardware reset clears the entire register to `$00`.
26383dbd [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Clearing Flags: Reading the associated Port A data register (`$E810`) automatically
26383dbd [gemini-3.7-flash] #resets Bits 6 and 7 back to `0`.
26383dbe [gemini-3.7-flash] #
