263b886b [glm-5.3] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 glm-5.3 Z 🪠 0.7° $0.223 398.2KB 124.24s
263b886b [glm-5.3] #Thanks — this is all new to me in this session, so a few observations across the three files.
263b886c [glm-5.3] #
263b886c [glm-5.3] #• On the trace (notes.txt)*
263b886c [glm-5.3] #
263b886c [glm-5.3] #The PET is alive and well: the IRQ chain (E66B → `JMP (0219)` → `INCTIME`) is ticking the jiffy
263b886d [glm-5.3] #clock at 0205 (D3→D4→D5→D6→D7), the cursor blink countdown at 0225 resets to 14, and the keyboard
263b886d [glm-5.3] #scan through PIA1_PA/PIA1_PB runs cleanly. The main thread, however, is parked in the polling loop
263b886d [glm-5.3] #at E297–E29D waiting for 020D to go non-zero, which never happens. Since the keyboard scan reads FF
263b886d [glm-5.3] #throughout, if 020D is the key buffer this is simply the machine idling for input — the emulator
263b886e [glm-5.3] #side (`readPetMatrix()`) would need to return real key bits to break it.
263b886e [glm-5.3] #
263b886e [glm-5.3] #One display convention worth knowing when reading these logs: in `branch()`, not-taken branches
263b886e [glm-5.3] #print the fall-through PC with a trailing ``, not the actual target. So `BNE E68D` at E68B
263b886f [glm-5.3] #is really "not taken, target was $E6B0". That makes the traces a little misleading at first glance.
263b886f [glm-5.3] #
263b886f [glm-5.3] #• Possible bugs in machine.ts*
263b886f [glm-5.3] #
263b8870 [glm-5.3] #- `epoch = Date.UTC(2026,10,8)` — JS months are 0-indexed, so this is 8 November 2026, not
263b8870 [glm-5.3] #8 August as the comment states. Should be month `7`.
263b8870 [glm-5.3] #- In `tickVic()`, `0x83|(joyFire)?0:0x20|(sense)?0:0x40|((joyDir&7)<<2)` — the ternary binds looser
263b8871 [glm-5.3] #than `|`, so this parses as `(0x83|joyFire) ? ...`, which is always truthy. `$9111` therefore
263b8871 [glm-5.3] #always gets written as 0, breaking the VIC-20 joystick entirely. Needs parentheses.
263b8871 [glm-5.3] #- `onInput` case `49` logs `sabotage.title` but the import is `appleSabotage` — a ReferenceError
263b8871 [glm-5.3] #waiting to happen.
263b8871 [glm-5.3] #- Opcode `0xAF` is mapped as a 2-byte `LDA (zp,X)`, but the genuine article there is LAX absolute
263b8872 [glm-5.3] #(3 bytes, illegal opcode). Fine if intentional for a specific title, but it will silently
263b8872 [glm-5.3] #misexecute anything expecting real 0xAF semantics.
263b8872 [glm-5.3] #- `missingCodes` is a `Set`, but `memCode()` uses bracket assignment and `reportMissing()` uses
263b8872 [glm-5.3] #`Object.keys()` — it happens to work via accidental property assignment, but `.add()` would be the
263b8873 [glm-5.3] #honest version.
263b8873 [glm-5.3] #- Dead-code hazards: `refreshCRT()` references an undefined `game`, and `displayApple1()` tests an
263b8873 [glm-5.3] #undefined `frame`. Both would throw if ever called.
263b8873 [glm-5.3] #
263b8874 [glm-5.3] #• Otherwise*
263b8874 [glm-5.3] #
