263c2acb [glm-5.3] #
263c2acb [glm-5.3] #The sign extension now happens before the target computation:
263c2acb [glm-5.3] #
263c2acc [glm-5.3] #- `offset` is sign-extended immediately after `get8()`, so `target=(pc+2+offset)&0xFFFF` is correct
263c2acc [glm-5.3] #for both taken and not-taken paths.
263c2acc [glm-5.3] #- Re-running the earlier trace example: `BEQ` at `E29A` with offset `FB` → `offset=-5` →
263c2acc [glm-5.3] #`target=E297`. The PET idle loop now cycles `E297–$E29D` as it should, with the jiffy IRQ
263c2acc [glm-5.3] #continuing to interleave.
263c2acd [glm-5.3] #- `branchBackwards(target, pc+2)` now receives the genuine destination rather than a recomputed
263c2acd [glm-5.3] #expression, and the `offset<0` condition is equivalent to the old `offset>127` check — loop
263c2acd [glm-5.3] #detection semantics are preserved.
263c2acd [glm-5.3] #- Cycle penalties remain right: +1 taken, +1 page-cross, both inside `if(taken)`.
263c2acd [glm-5.3] #- The display convention is now the good one — true target always, `*` marking not-taken.
263c2ace [glm-5.3] #
263c2ace [glm-5.3] #One exotic non-issue for the record: a forward branch near `$FFFF` that wraps past the top of
263c2ace [glm-5.3] #memory produces `target < pc` with a positive offset, so `branchBackwards` won't fire. That's
263c2ace [glm-5.3] #arguably the correct call for loop detection anyway.
263c2acf [glm-5.3] #
263c2acf [glm-5.3] #• Still outstanding from last round*
