263f8906 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Here is an analysis of the implementation, highlighting the key 6520 PIA and 6522 VIA behaviours
263f8906 [gemini-3.7-flash] #that need adjustments.
263f8906 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
263f8906 [gemini-3.7-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
263f8907 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
263f8907 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Key Areas to Address
263f8907 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
263f8907 [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. Missing DDRB handling on PIA 1 (`E812` / `E813`)
263f8908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• On the 6520 PIA, Port B uses the exact same multiplexing mechanism as Port A.
263f8908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• When bit 2 of `CRB` (`E813`) is `0`, `E812` accesses the Data Direction Register B (`DDRB`).
263f8908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• When bit 2 of `CRB` is `1`, `$E812` accesses the Output/Input Register B.
263f8908 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• The PET startup ROM initializes both `DDRA` and `DDRB`. Without `ddrb` handling, writes to
263f8909 [gemini-3.7-flash] #configure Port B may be lost.
263f8909 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
263f8909 [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. Interrupt Flag Clearing (Bits 6 & 7)
263f8909 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Reading the peripheral data register (`PRA` / `PRB`) clears the interrupt flags in the respective
263f890a [gemini-3.7-flash] #control register (`CRA` / `CRB`).
263f890a [gemini-3.7-flash] #• However, reading the Direction Register (`DDRA` / `DDRB`) must not clear the interrupt
263f890a [gemini-3.7-flash] #flags. The flag clearing should only happen when `(controlRegister & 0x04) !== 0`.
263f890a [gemini-3.7-flash] #
263f890b [gemini-3.7-flash] #3. Control Register 2 (`$E813`) Write Filtering
263f890b [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Just like `E811` (`CRA`), bits 6 and 7 of `E813` (`CRB`) are read-only interrupt flags set by
263f890b [gemini-3.7-flash] #CB1/CB2 transitions. Writes should preserve bits 6 and 7 while updating bits 0–5.
263f890b [gemini-3.7-flash] #
263f890c [gemini-3.7-flash] #4. VIA Video Blanking (`$E840`)
263f890c [gemini-3.7-flash] #• `$E840` is VIA 6522 Port B. Bit 5 reflects the video blanking/retrace state.
263f890c [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Make sure other pins on Port B (such as cassette or user port pins) remain stable when updating
263f890c [gemini-3.7-flash] #bit 5.
