264069fb [gemini-3.7-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.054 164.1KB 11.93s
264069fb [gemini-3.7-flash] #Here are the key observations, architecture notes, and subtle hardware details noted in this
264069fb [gemini-3.7-flash] #version of `machine.ts`:
264069fb [gemini-3.7-flash] #
264069fc [gemini-3.7-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
264069fc [gemini-3.7-flash] #
264069fc [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. Architectural Highlights
264069fc [gemini-3.7-flash] #
264069fd [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Unified Multi-Machine Framework:
264069fd [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * The single 6502 core handles multiple targets (Apple II/II+, Commodore PET, VIC-20, C64,
264069fd [gemini-3.7-flash] #Plus/4, Atari DVG vector arcade, and Ben Eater 6502 kit) via target-specific bus dispatches
264069fd [gemini-3.7-flash] #(`readPET`, `readVIC`, `readC64CIA`, `readAddressBus`, etc.).
264069fe [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Audio & Vector Engines:
264069fe [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * Loudspeaker: Tracks cycle timestamps between `$C030` accesses, converting delta cycles
264069fe [gemini-3.7-flash] #to 48 kHz PCM buffers for native output.
264069fe [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * Cassette/Datasette: Cycle-accurate pulse recording and WAV file edge decoding via
264069ff [gemini-3.7-flash] #`CassetteRecorder`.
264069ff [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * DVG (Digital Vector Generator): Hardware interpreter supporting Atari vector opcodes
264069ff [gemini-3.7-flash] #(`LABS`, `SVEC`, `VEC`, `JSRL`, `RTSL`, `JMP`, `HALT`) invoked via memory strobe at `$3000`.
264069ff [gemini-3.7-flash] #• ANSI & Braille Terminal Display Pipeline:
26406a00 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * Uses 2×4 Braille glyph mapping (`brailleDisplay` / `displayAppleHires`) for bitmap graphics and
26406a00 [gemini-3.7-flash] #LCD rendering directly inside terminal grids.
26406a00 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * PETSCII and Apple 40-column text modes are rendered using full-width Unicode characters with
26406a00 [gemini-3.7-flash] #ANSI 256-color attribute sequences.
26406a01 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
26406a01 [gemini-3.7-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
26406a01 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
26406a01 [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. Notable 6502 CPU Implementations
26406a02 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
26406a02 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Indirect JMP Hardware Bug Emulation (`$6C`):
26406a02 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * Correctly replicates the page-boundary wrapping bug on NMOS 6502:
26406a02 [gemini-3.7-flash] #    `const highAddress = (pointer & 0xFF00) | ((pointer + 1) & 0x00FF);`
26406a03 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Status Register Stack Operations (`PHP` / `PLP` / `BRK` / `RTI`):
26406a03 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * `PLP` and `RTI` correctly set bit 5 (`ST |= 0x20`) and clear bit 4 (Break flag is not stored in
26406a03 [gemini-3.7-flash] #the physical register).
26406a04 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * `BRK` properly sets both bit 4 and bit 5 when pushing `ST` to the stack.
26406a04 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Apple II Soft Switch Writes:
26406a04 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * In `writeAddress()`, Apple II addresses in the `C000–C0FF` range invoke
26406a04 [gemini-3.7-flash] #`this.readAddress(address)`, faithfully reflecting that physical Apple II hardware triggers soft
26406a05 [gemini-3.7-flash] #switches on any bus access (read or write).
26406a05 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
26406a05 [gemini-3.7-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
26406a05 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
26406a06 [gemini-3.7-flash] #3. Edge Cases to Keep in Mind
26406a06 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
26406a06 [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. `PHP` Stack Byte (Bit 5):
26406a06 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * On NMOS 6502, `PHP` pushes `ST | 0x30` (both bit 4 Break and bit 5 Unused are pushed as `1`).
26406a07 [gemini-3.7-flash] #In `case 0x08`, only `0x10` is explicitly ORed. Adding `| 0x30` ensures strict compliance if
26406a07 [gemini-3.7-flash] #diagnostics check bit 5 on pull.
26406a07 [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. Page Boundary Crossing Cycles on Writes:
26406a07 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * In `targetAbsoluteX()`, extra cycle penalties are counted on page crossings. On genuine 6502
26406a08 [gemini-3.7-flash] #hardware, instructions that perform a read before write (e.g., `INC`, `DEC`, `ASL`, `ROR`) or plain
26406a08 [gemini-3.7-flash] #stores (`STA abs,X`) always take the maximum cycles regardless of whether a page boundary is
26406a08 [gemini-3.7-flash] #crossed.
26406a08 [gemini-3.7-flash] #3. Decimal Mode Flag Setting (`ADC` / `SBC`):
26406a09 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * On NMOS 6502, `N` and `Z` flags reflect the binary addition result rather than the
26406a09 [gemini-3.7-flash] #BCD-corrected accumulator value. The current implementation sets flags post-correction
26406a09 [gemini-3.7-flash] #(`setStatus(result & 0xFF)`), which is standard for CMOS 65C02 but differs slightly on NMOS
26406a09 [gemini-3.7-flash] #hardware.
26406a0a [gemini-3.7-flash] #
