2641cc66 [nitro@ryzen5] is break key on pet a normal key, and does it stop basic
2641ccbb [gemini-3.7-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.010 27.45KB 4.91s
2641ccbb [gemini-3.7-flash] #Yes to both:
2641ccbb [gemini-3.7-flash] #
2641ccbb [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. Is it a normal key?
2641ccbb [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Yes. Unlike later machines such as the Commodore 64 or VIC-20 (which had a dedicated
2641ccbb [gemini-3.7-flash] #hardware `RESTORE` line wired directly to the CPU's Non-Maskable Interrupt), the
2641ccbc [gemini-3.7-flash] #`RUN/STOP`* key on the PET is simply a standard switch in the standard keyboard matrix
2641ccbc [gemini-3.7-flash] #(scanned via the 6520 PIA chip during the regular 60 Hz interrupt). It has no special electrical
2641ccbc [gemini-3.7-flash] #connection or dedicated hardware interrupt.
2641ccbc [gemini-3.7-flash] #
2641ccbd [gemini-3.7-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2641ccbd [gemini-3.7-flash] #
2641ccbd [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. Does it stop BASIC?
2641ccbd [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Yes.* While a BASIC program executes, the PET Kernal checks the keyboard matrix buffer.
2641ccbe [gemini-3.7-flash] #If it detects that `RUN/STOP` is pressed:
2641ccbe [gemini-3.7-flash] #
2641ccbe [gemini-3.7-flash] #• It immediately halts program execution.
2641ccbe [gemini-3.7-flash] #• It prints:
2641ccbf [gemini-3.7-flash] #
2641ccbf [gemini-3.7-flash] #  BREAK IN LINE <number>
2641ccbf [gemini-3.7-flash] #  READY.
2641ccbf [gemini-3.7-flash] #
2641ccc0 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• You can resume execution from where it stopped by typing `CONT` and pressing `RETURN`.
2641ccc0 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
2641ccc0 [gemini-3.7-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2641ccc0 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
2641ccc1 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Additional Behavior:
2641ccc1 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Unshifted: Acts as `STOP` (interrupts BASIC execution or stops screen
2641ccc1 [gemini-3.7-flash] #listing/scrolling).
2641ccc2 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Shifted (`Shift + RUN/STOP`): Acts as `RUN` (initiates a tape `LOAD` and
2641ccc2 [gemini-3.7-flash] #automatically issues `RUN` upon completion).
