264e6a0e [gemini-3.7-flash] #On the Commodore Plus/4 (and related 264-series machines such as the C16 and C116), address
264e6a0e [gemini-3.7-flash] #`FD20` (64800 decimal) resides in the upper KERNAL ROM region (E000–$FFFF).
264e6a0f [gemini-3.7-flash] #
264e6a0f [gemini-3.7-flash] #Context and Function
264e6a0f [gemini-3.7-flash] #
264e6a0f [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Subsystem: Cassette (Datasette) Handling
264e6a0f [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Function: In the standard Plus/4 KERNAL ROM, `$FD20` is an internal routine used for
264e6a10 [gemini-3.7-flash] #low-level tape I/O operations (part of the tape block read and header search routines).
264e6a10 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
264e6a10 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Considerations
264e6a10 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
264e6a11 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Because `FD20` is an internal KERNAL routine rather than a standardized jump table entry (which are
264e6a11 [gemini-3.7-flash] #located from `FF81` to `FFF5`), its exact position and behaviour can vary across different KERNAL
264e6a11 [gemini-3.7-flash] #revisions (e.g., PAL vs. NTSC revisions or custom ROMs). For cassette operations in software, it is
264e6a11 [gemini-3.7-flash] #generally recommended to interface via the official KERNAL vectors (such as `LOAD` at `FFD5` or
264e6a12 [gemini-3.7-flash] #`SAVE` at `$FFD8`).
264e6a12 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
