264f9ca7 [gemini-3.7-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 gemini-3.7-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.017 43.76KB 8.69s
264f9ca7 [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. `$FD01 00` (MOS 6551 ACIA Reset)
264f9ca8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Address `$FD01` is the Status / Programmed Reset Register of the MOS 6551 ACIA
264f9ca8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #(the RS-232 serial chip).
264f9ca8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Writing `$00` performs a software reset on the ACIA to clear its internal state, parity, and
264f9ca8 [gemini-3.7-flash] #framing error flags.
264f9ca9 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
264f9ca9 [gemini-3.7-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
264f9ca9 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
264f9ca9 [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. `$FF08` Keyboard Matrix Reads
264f9caa [gemini-3.7-flash] #• `$FF08` is the TED Keyboard Latch / Row register.
264f9caa [gemini-3.7-flash] #• The KERNAL reads this register immediately after initializing hardware to check for special boot
264f9caa [gemini-3.7-flash] #keys (such as the `STOP` or `C=` keys) to determine whether to abort normal startup or enter the
264f9caa [gemini-3.7-flash] #machine code monitor.
264f9caa [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Returning `7F` (or `FF` when no keys are pressed) indicates no boot-override keys are held down.
264f9cab [gemini-3.7-flash] #
264f9cab [gemini-3.7-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
264f9cab [gemini-3.7-flash] #
264f9cab [gemini-3.7-flash] #3. The `FFFD` \rightarrow `FFF6` Read / Write Sequence
264f9cac [gemini-3.7-flash] #This sequence is the KERNAL copying the hardware vectors and Reset trampolines from ROM into
264f9cac [gemini-3.7-flash] #the underlying RAM:
264f9cac [gemini-3.7-flash] #
264f9cac [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Why it does this:
264f9cad [gemini-3.7-flash] #  When the Plus/4 switches out ROM to enable full 64KB RAM mode (via `FF3F`), the CPU still needs
264f9cad [gemini-3.7-flash] #valid reset/interrupt vectors (`FFFA–FFFF`) and bank-switching code at `FFF6` in memory so an
264f9cad [gemini-3.7-flash] #interrupt or switch back does not crash the system.
264f9cae [gemini-3.7-flash] #
264f9cae [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Memory Architecture Note:
264f9cae [gemini-3.7-flash] #  In the Commodore architecture, when ROM is enabled:
264f9cae [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * Reads from `FFF6–FFFF` fetch data from the KERNAL ROM.
264f9cae [gemini-3.7-flash] #  * Writes to `FFF6–FFFF` pass directly through to the underlying RAM.
264f9caf [gemini-3.7-flash] #
264f9caf [gemini-3.7-flash] #  The loop reads the vector table from ROM (`LDA FFF6,X`) and writes it immediately back (`STA
264f9caf [gemini-3.7-flash] #FFF6,X`), thereby copying the ROM vectors into the RAM underneath.
264f9caf [gemini-3.7-flash] #
