264fa6b3 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Bit Breakdown
264fa6b3 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
264fa6b4 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Page Filter (`address & 0xFD00 == 0xFD00`):
264fa6b4 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  Isolates pages `%11111101` (`FD`) and `%11111111` (`FF`) in a single mask check.
264fa6b4 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Page Selector (`address & 0x0200`):
264fa6b4 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  Checks bit 9 (`0` for `FDxx`, `1` for `FFxx`).
264fa6b5 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• `FD00–FDDF` Decoding (`(address & 0x00E0) != 0x00E0`):
264fa6b5 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  `FDE0–FDFF` has the top three bits (`%111x_xxxx`) set. Inverting this condition isolates `00–DF`.
264fa6b5 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• `FF00–FF3F` Decoding (`(address & 0x00C0) == 0x0000`):
264fa6b6 [gemini-3.7-flash] #  The lower 64 bytes (`00–3F`) have bits 7 and 6 cleared (`%00xx_xxxx`).
264fa6b6 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
