264ffe35 [gemini-3.7-flash] #F350: LDA $FFF6,X   ; Read vector from ROM
264ffe35 [gemini-3.7-flash] #F353: STA $FFF6,X   ; Write vector to RAM
264ffe35 [gemini-3.7-flash] #F356: DEX
264ffe36 [gemini-3.7-flash] #F357: BPL $F350
264ffe36 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
264ffe36 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
264ffe36 [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. Why these writes must succeed:
264ffe37 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   Immediately after this loop, the KERNAL performs the RAM sizing routine (`$F359`).
264ffe37 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   To test total available RAM, it writes `$FF3F` (switching the CPU to 100% all-RAM mode,
264ffe37 [gemini-3.7-flash] #disabling the KERNAL ROM).
264ffe37 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   It then executes code out of high memory and triggers routines via the reset/NMI vectors at
264ffe38 [gemini-3.7-flash] #`FFFA–FFFF`.
264ffe38 [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. The Result:
264ffe38 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   If the writes to `FFF6–FFFF` were blocked, dropped, or treated as read-only ROM writes, then
264ffe38 [gemini-3.7-flash] #when `FF3F` switches to all-RAM mode, `FFF6–FFFF` contains uninitialized garbage (`00` or random
264ffe39 [gemini-3.7-flash] #data). The CPU jumps to `$0000` or an invalid address on the very next instruction or interrupt,
264ffe39 [gemini-3.7-flash] #causing a silent crash before the display screen is initialized or cleared.
264ffe39 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
264ffe39 [gemini-3.7-flash] #━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
264ffe3a [gemini-3.7-flash] #
264ffe3a [gemini-3.7-flash] #Verification Checklist for your Memory Controller
264ffe3a [gemini-3.7-flash] #
264ffe3a [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. Check write permission on `FF40–FFFF` when ROM is active:
264ffe3b [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * When `ROM_ENABLED` is true, reads from `FFF6–FFFF` return ROM data, but writes to
264ffe3b [gemini-3.7-flash] #`FFF6–FFFF` must write directly into underlying RAM.
264ffe3b [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. Check the `FF3E / FF3F` Strobes:
264ffe3b [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * Writing any value to `$FF3E` must set `ROM_ENABLED = true`.
264ffe3c [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * Writing any value to `FF3F` must set `ROM_ENABLED = false` (all reads & writes map to RAM,
264ffe3c [gemini-3.7-flash] #except `FD00–FDDF` and `FF00–$FF3F` which remain I/O).
264ffe3c [gemini-3.7-flash] #3. RAM writes in `is_io_address()`:
264ffe3c [gemini-3.7-flash] #   * Ensure `FFF6–FFFF` returns `false` from `is_io_address()` so the write handler routes the data
264ffe3d [gemini-3.7-flash] #into the system RAM array rather than discarding it as unmapped I/O.
264ffe3d [gemini-3.7-flash] #
