26d2ec81 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #
26d2ec81 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #Why it matters for your desktop manager
26d2ec81 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #
26d2ec81 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #Currently your `graphemeWidth()` function makes an educated guess that a ZWJ emoji sequence
26d2ec82 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #occupies 2 cells. If the terminal supports mode 2027, that guess becomes exactly
26d2ec82 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #correct — the terminal will render the cluster as a single wide character instead of a sequence
26d2ec82 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #of separate emoji.
26d2ec82 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #
26d2ec83 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #This alignment is important because:
26d2ec83 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #
26d2ec83 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #- If your `stringWidth` says a cluster is wide (2 cells) but the terminal renders it as multiple
26d2ec83 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #narrow characters, your box drawing will be off.
26d2ec83 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #- If the terminal honors mode 2027, then both your width calculation and the terminal’s rendering
26d2ec84 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #agree.
26d2ec84 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #
26d2ec84 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #Without mode 2027, older terminals may render `👨‍👩‍👧‍👦` as four separate emoji, each taking 2
26d2ec84 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #cells (total 8), while your code says 2. That mismatch causes broken borders and misaligned text.
26d2ec84 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #
26d2ec85 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #Should we enable it?
