26d366d0 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #now, just enabling the mode is the pragmatic approach.
26d366d1 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #
26d366d1 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #Why this handles your 4‑head example well
26d366d1 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #
26d366d1 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #With `Intl.Segmenter`, `👨‍👩‍👧‍👦` is returned as a single grapheme. Our `graphemeWidth` sees the
26d366d2 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #ZWJ and returns `2`. If the terminal supports mode 2027, it will render as one wide glyph — so 2
26d366d2 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #cells is correct. If it doesn’t, the terminal may render four separate emoji (8 cells), and your
26d366d2 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #layout will be off. That’s the residual risk, which you can mitigate with the constant as
26d366d2 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #suggested.
26d366d3 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #
26d366d3 [deepseek-v4-flash-vision] #Let me know if you need any adjustments or if you’d like a sample detection routine.
