26e643f0 [glm-5.3-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 glm-5.3-flash Z 🪠 0.7° $0.001 21.74KB 68.95s
26e643f0 [glm-5.3-flash] #Thanks for sharing — this is a neat little codebase. A few observations on things that stood out:
26e643f1 [glm-5.3-flash] #
26e643f1 [glm-5.3-flash] #• Possible bugs*
26e643f1 [glm-5.3-flash] #
26e643f1 [glm-5.3-flash] #- In `pollKeypad()`, Home and End look swapped: `case "[H"` sets `EndBit` and `case "[F"` sets
26e643f2 [glm-5.3-flash] #`HomeBit`. Most terminals send `[H` for Home and `[F` for End (matching the C1 codes
26e643f2 [glm-5.3-flash] #`[1;H`/`[1;F`). If this was deliberate for a specific terminal, worth a comment saying so.
26e643f2 [glm-5.3-flash] #- The `KeyBits` enum counts from zero (`UP=0, DOWN=1…`) so its members don't align with the
26e643f2 [glm-5.3-flash] #`UpBit=1, DownBit=2…` mask constants actually used below. The inline comments also repeat values
26e643f3 [glm-5.3-flash] #(`// 64 128` appears twice, and `SPACE,SHIFT` reuses the `// 16 32` pair). Since the enum isn't
26e643f3 [glm-5.3-flash] #referenced anywhere, it may be misleading rather than useful in its current form.
26e643f3 [glm-5.3-flash] #- SGR mouse parsing discards the `M`/`m` press/release terminator (it survives as text attached to
26e643f3 [glm-5.3-flash] #the last coordinate, harmlessly ignored by `parseInt`). As a workaround you XOR-toggle the button
26e643f4 [glm-5.3-flash] #bits, which roughly works — but `case 32` will fire on every motion event while a button is held
26e643f4 [glm-5.3-flash] #(SGR adds 32 for motion), so `MouseRightBit` will flicker rapidly during drags. Distinguishing
26e643f4 [glm-5.3-flash] #press from release needs that trailing character.
26e643f4 [glm-5.3-flash] #- `mouseButtons |= 4` for motion is never cleared, so the motion bit latches on permanently after
26e643f5 [glm-5.3-flash] #the first move.
26e643f5 [glm-5.3-flash] #- Escape sequences split across two stdin reads (common over SSH) will fail to parse. Buffering
26e643f5 [glm-5.3-flash] #partial reads until a complete sequence arrives would harden this.
26e643f5 [glm-5.3-flash] #
26e643f6 [glm-5.3-flash] #• Smaller notes*
26e643f6 [glm-5.3-flash] #
26e643f6 [glm-5.3-flash] #- `inputTask` is stored but never awaited, so a rejection in `runInputTask` could go unobserved.
26e643f6 [glm-5.3-flash] #- `class panel` with `rect: Uint16Array` and no initializer will trip
26e643f7 [glm-5.3-flash] #`strictPropertyInitialization` if you ever run `deno check`.
26e643f7 [glm-5.3-flash] #- `GRAPHEME_DISABLE` is sent at boot even though `terminal.ts` carries fairly careful
26e643f7 [glm-5.3-flash] #grapheme-width logic — I assume that's intentional because mode 2027 interferes with your manual
26e643f7 [glm-5.3-flash] #cell layout?
26e643f7 [glm-5.3-flash] #- Dead weight: `hex()`, `fadePumps()`'s return value, `oldKeys` change detection, and the
26e643f8 [glm-5.3-flash] #commented-out `gridHalfWindowLayer` call referencing functions that don't exist yet.
26e643f8 [glm-5.3-flash] #
26e643f8 [glm-5.3-flash] #• On the README todo* — "basic mouse color grid" fits nicely with what's already plumbed:
26e643f8 [glm-5.3-flash] #`mousePosition` and the motion bit in `hitBits` give you everything needed to paint cells under the
26e643f9 [glm-5.3-flash] #cursor into a half-block grid, once `updateConsole` grows a real renderer.
26e643f9 [glm-5.3-flash] #
26e643f9 [glm-5.3-flash] #Happy to dig into the platform-specific FFI/MIDI modules next, or sketch the color-grid renderer
26e643f9 [glm-5.3-flash] #whenever you're ready.
26e643fa [glm-5.3-flash] #
