26e71128 [glm-5.3-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.1 glm-5.3-flash Z 🪠 0.7° $0.001 17.06KB 76.35s
26e71128 [glm-5.3-flash] #Thanks for sharing — here's a read-through of what stands out, both new material and a few rough
26e71128 [glm-5.3-flash] #edges worth knowing about.
26e71129 [glm-5.3-flash] #
26e71129 [glm-5.3-flash] #stringwidth.ts
26e71129 [glm-5.3-flash] #
26e7112a [glm-5.3-flash] #- Blocking issue: line 5 contains a stray token, `Intl.localesargument`, sitting as a bare
26e7112a [glm-5.3-flash] #statement. It reads like a research note that landed inside code, but `deno check` will reject the
26e7112a [glm-5.3-flash] #file until it's removed or commented out.
26e7112a [glm-5.3-flash] #- The two-pass design is solid: `Intl.Segmenter` for cluster boundaries, then your own width rules
26e7112a [glm-5.3-flash] #per cluster. This pairs directly with the README's EAW research — you're effectively
26e7112a [glm-5.3-flash] #hand-implementing F/W, treating H/Na/N as narrow, and leaving A (Ambiguous) unhandled, which
26e7112b [glm-5.3-flash] #matches the docs' open question. An option flag for ambiguous-wide terminals could slot in later.
26e7112b [glm-5.3-flash] #- Coverage gaps to be aware of: variation selectors (U+FE00–FE0F) aren't in the zero-width set, so
26e7112b [glm-5.3-flash] #🏳️ falls through to the `wideCount > 1` heuristic rather than explicit handling. Regional
26e7112b [glm-5.3-flash] #indicators (U+1F1E6–1F1FF) sit below your emoji range start, but flag pairs sum to 2
26e7112c [glm-5.3-flash] #anyway, so results stay correct by coincidence. Hangul Jamo Extended-A/B ranges are also absent.
26e7112c [glm-5.3-flash] #
26e7112c [glm-5.3-flash] #mazgui.ts
26e7112c [glm-5.3-flash] #
26e7112c [glm-5.3-flash] #- The gadget taxonomy (`GADGET_`, `ACTIVATE_`, `LAYOUT_*`) is clearly Intuition-flavoured —
26e7112d [glm-5.3-flash] #nice lineage for an "ANSI desktop manager."
26e7112d [glm-5.3-flash] #- The inertial pointer physics (velocity accumulation, friction decay, soft clamping against a
26e7112d [glm-5.3-flash] #1024×1024 virtual grid) is a distinctive touch. Note `updateCursor` is currently commented out of
26e7112e [glm-5.3-flash] #the loop, so pan values stay pinned at zero.
26e7112e [glm-5.3-flash] #- There's a meaningful interaction between mode 2027 and your own segmenter: you print
26e7112e [glm-5.3-flash] #`GRAPHEME_DISABLE` at startup, which means the terminal will move its real cursor per code point,
26e7112e [glm-5.3-flash] #not per cluster. Your `stringWidth` compensates arithmetically, but any place you emit text and
26e7112e [glm-5.3-flash] #then reposition relative to it may drift on wide glyphs. Worth keeping the two strategies
26e7112e [glm-5.3-flash] #consciously opposed rather than accidental.
26e7112f [glm-5.3-flash] #- `updateConsole` computes `w`/`h` and receives `panx`/`pany` but uses none of them yet — clearly
26e7112f [glm-5.3-flash] #scaffolding for the half-block layer (`appHeight*2` hints at ▀/▄ double-row rendering, which suits
26e7112f [glm-5.3-flash] #the "mouse color grid" todo nicely).
26e7112f [glm-5.3-flash] #- Minor: `cursorRestore` is named as DECRC but holds SGR reset (`\x1b[0m`); actual restore lives in
26e71130 [glm-5.3-flash] #time.ts as `CursorPop`. Renaming one of them would prevent future confusion.
26e71130 [glm-5.3-flash] #
26e71130 [glm-5.3-flash] #time.ts
26e71130 [glm-5.3-flash] #
26e71130 [glm-5.3-flash] #- Midnight bug: `((h>12)?(h-12):h)` yields 0 at midnight; a 12-hour clock conventionally
26e71131 [glm-5.3-flash] #shows 12 there.
26e71131 [glm-5.3-flash] #- `toWideDigits(num, 2)` passes a second argument the function doesn't accept — harmless today,
26e71131 [glm-5.3-flash] #misleading later.
26e71132 [glm-5.3-flash] #- The manually typed `fullWidth` table is elegant documentation but unused (`wideNumber` does the
26e71132 [glm-5.3-flash] #work), and it duplicates data derivable via `String.fromCharCode(0xFF10 + n)`. Same for
26e71132 [glm-5.3-flash] #`fillEmoji`. The header comment still says `clock.ts` while the file is `time.ts`.
26e71132 [glm-5.3-flash] #
26e71132 [glm-5.3-flash] #language.ts
26e71133 [glm-5.3-flash] #
26e71133 [glm-5.3-flash] #- Extracting UTC offsets by slicing `" GMT"` out of `toLocaleString` output is clever but
26e71133 [glm-5.3-flash] #locale-coupled — pinning `"en"` as you do is what keeps it safe. The `||"+0"` fallback for Zone 0
26e71133 [glm-5.3-flash] #is a tidy detail.
26e71133 [glm-5.3-flash] #
26e71133 [glm-5.3-flash] #Overall
26e71134 [glm-5.3-flash] #
26e71134 [glm-5.3-flash] #The through-line is coherent: README research → width engine → desktop manager, with the family
26e71134 [glm-5.3-flash] #emoji in the window title doubling as a live regression test for the ZWJ path. The immediate
26e71134 [glm-5.3-flash] #practical item is the stray identifier in stringwidth.ts; everything else is scaffold waiting for
26e71134 [glm-5.3-flash] #the mouse-grid work.
26e71135 [glm-5.3-flash] #
