2702337c [glm-5.3-flash] #Thanks for sharing this, Simon. I don't have a prior version to diff against, so here are general
2702337d [glm-5.3-flash] #observations from a fresh read, roughly in order of severity.
2702337d [glm-5.3-flash] #
2702337d [glm-5.3-flash] #• Compile blockers*
2702337d [glm-5.3-flash] #
2702337e [glm-5.3-flash] #- The global `const int *gpio=[0,1,2,...]` at the top isn't valid C++ — square-bracket array
2702337e [glm-5.3-flash] #literals don't exist here, and the pointer is never used anyway. It needs brace initialisation (or
2702337e [glm-5.3-flash] #a `std::vector`), or removal.
2702337e [glm-5.3-flash] #- Inside the `#ifdef HAS_ROM` branch of `picoInstance()` there's a truncated loop: `for(int
2702337f [glm-5.3-flash] #i=0;i<)`. Note that only `USE_ROM` is defined at the top, so this branch currently never compiles —
2702337f [glm-5.3-flash] #but the `USE_ROM`/`HAS_ROM` name mismatch looks accidental, and the moment someone defines
2702337f [glm-5.3-flash] #`HAS_ROM` the build breaks.
27023380 [glm-5.3-flash] #- The `READ_PS2` block calls `flush()`, which doesn't exist — the function here is `flushComs()`.
27023380 [glm-5.3-flash] #Dormant while the define is commented out, but worth fixing.
27023380 [glm-5.3-flash] #- `updateRPC()` is defined unconditionally but calls `cdcReadLine()` and friends that only exist
27023380 [glm-5.3-flash] #under `USE_CDC`. Non-CDC builds will likely fail at link time; the function should sit inside the
27023381 [glm-5.3-flash] #same conditional.
27023381 [glm-5.3-flash] #
27023381 [glm-5.3-flash] #• Runtime / correctness*
27023381 [glm-5.3-flash] #
27023382 [glm-5.3-flash] #- In `updateRPC()`, the result of `parser.parseJSON()` is ignored and `payload` is dereferenced
27023382 [glm-5.3-flash] #immediately. Malformed JSON will crash the device — worth checking both the status and the pointer
27023382 [glm-5.3-flash] #before use.
27023382 [glm-5.3-flash] #- On RP2350, `setTime()` always calls `aon_timer_start()`. That will succeed once, then fail on
27023383 [glm-5.3-flash] #every subsequent `rtc.set` RPC because the timer is already running. You probably want the
27023383 [glm-5.3-flash] #start/set split (you have the right call commented out).
27023383 [glm-5.3-flash] #- Boot sequence oddity: `rtcGood=setTime(0)` is immediately undone by the hardcoded 2021
27023384 [glm-5.3-flash] #`rtc_set_datetime` in the `HAS_RTC` block, so the initial set is pointless and `wallTime()` starts
27023384 [glm-5.3-flash] #at 2021 regardless.
27023384 [glm-5.3-flash] #- `popCommandQueue()` takes `back()` and `pop_back()` — that's a stack, not a queue. If ordering
27023384 [glm-5.3-flash] #matters, it's processing commands in reverse.
27023385 [glm-5.3-flash] #- `locallog` grows without bound; on a long-running device that's slow heap exhaustion. A cap or
27023385 [glm-5.3-flash] #ring buffer would be safer.
27023385 [glm-5.3-flash] #- The main loop calls `adc_select_input()`/`adc_read()` unconditionally, but `adc_init()` only runs
27023385 [glm-5.3-flash] #under `USE_PADDLES` or `HAS_ADC`, neither of which is defined here. Does something in a header
27023386 [glm-5.3-flash] #initialise the ADC?
27023386 [glm-5.3-flash] #- `fire` and `keys` set bits when the pin reads high, but the pins are pulled up with
27023386 [glm-5.3-flash] #pressed = low, so the on-screen indicators look inverted. Related: `apress`/`bpress` are computed
27023386 [glm-5.3-flash] #and never used.
27023386 [glm-5.3-flash] #- `initSD()` is defined but never called.
27023387 [glm-5.3-flash] #- `vidbit.set` echoes title/about back but never stores them — `picoTitle` is unchanged. Incomplete
27023387 [glm-5.3-flash] #feature, or intentional stub?
27023388 [glm-5.3-flash] #- `writeCDC()` can spin forever if the host disconnects between the `tud_cdc_connected()` check and
27023388 [glm-5.3-flash] #the write loop. Also, in `cdcReceiveCallback`, `charCount` isn't reset on the overflow path, so the
27023388 [glm-5.3-flash] #next line continues mid-buffer.
27023388 [glm-5.3-flash] #
27023389 [glm-5.3-flash] #• Smaller things*
27023389 [glm-5.3-flash] #
27023389 [glm-5.3-flash] #- Indentation mixes tabs and spaces (the RP2350 `setTime` body is spaces; the stray 2026
27023389 [glm-5.3-flash] #`datetime_t` block is a single space). Tabs throughout would keep it consistent.
2702338a [glm-5.3-flash] #- Dead code: `t1`/`t2`, `memmode`, `mask`, `address`, `refMilliVolt`, `adcONE`, the unused 2026
2702338a [glm-5.3-flash] #`datetime_t` in the RP2040 `setTime`, and the `PicoBeep`/`Host` types have no instances in this
2702338a [glm-5.3-flash] #file.
2702338a [glm-5.3-flash] #- Duplicate includes: `tusb.h`, `<iostream>`, `<iomanip>`, `<sstream>`.
2702338b [glm-5.3-flash] #- The `dotw` conversion maps to Monday-first, which contradicts the "0 is Sunday" comment in the
2702338b [glm-5.3-flash] #nearby example block.
2702338b [glm-5.3-flash] #- JSON responses interpolate strings without escaping, so any quote in `message` produces invalid
2702338c [glm-5.3-flash] #JSON. Unknown RPC methods also get no response at all where `-32601` would be conventional.
2702338c [glm-5.3-flash] #- `void log(const char*)` overloads `std::log` from `<math.h>` — it resolves fine, but it's a
2702338c [glm-5.3-flash] #surprise waiting for a reader.
2702338c [glm-5.3-flash] #
2702338d [glm-5.3-flash] #Happy to sketch fixes for any of these if you'd like — the parseJSON null check and the aon_timer
2702338d [glm-5.3-flash] #start/set split would be my first picks.
2702338d [glm-5.3-flash] #
