2702a8e3 [glm-5.3-flash] #uint32_t all = gpio_get_all();
2702a8e4 [glm-5.3-flash] #if(all & (1u<<KEY0_PIN)) { ... }
2702a8e4 [glm-5.3-flash] #
2702a8e4 [glm-5.3-flash] #
2702a8e4 [glm-5.3-flash] #Because it's a single SIO register read, every pin is sampled at the same instant — unlike four
2702a8e5 [glm-5.3-flash] #separate `gpio_get()` calls, which can straddle a pin change. That matters for anything where the
2702a8e5 [glm-5.3-flash] #pins are related, like your key/fire groups.
2702a8e5 [glm-5.3-flash] #
2702a8e5 [glm-5.3-flash] #For your `keys` byte specifically, if KEY0–KEY3 are contiguous pins, it's a mask and shift:
