2702e0b7 [glm-5.3-flash] #The Waveshare 1.14" is an ST7789 panel, 240×135, 4-wire SPI. The standalone module has 8 signal
2702e0b7 [glm-5.3-flash] #pins (on the 16-pin header, pins 9–16 are all just GND):
2702e0b7 [glm-5.3-flash] #
2702e0b8 [glm-5.3-flash] #╭──────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────╮
2702e0b8 [glm-5.3-flash] #│  Module pin  │  Function                        │  Maps to your code           │
2702e0b8 [glm-5.3-flash] #├──────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────┤
2702e0b8 [glm-5.3-flash] #│  VCC         │  3.3V supply                     │  3V3                         │
2702e0b9 [glm-5.3-flash] #│  GND         │  ground                          │  GND                         │
2702e0b9 [glm-5.3-flash] #│  DIN         │  SPI MOSI                        │  `LCD_MOSI_PIN`              │
2702e0b9 [glm-5.3-flash] #│  CLK         │  SPI SCK                         │  `LCD_CLK_PIN`               │
2702e0b9 [glm-5.3-flash] #│  CS          │  LCD chip select, active low     │  `LCD_CS_PIN`                │
2702e0ba [glm-5.3-flash] #│  DC          │  data/command select             │  `LCD_DC_PIN`                │
2702e0ba [glm-5.3-flash] #│  RST         │  reset, active low               │  `LCD_RST_PIN`               │
2702e0ba [glm-5.3-flash] #│  BL          │  backlight, high = on, PWM-able  │  `LCD_BL_PIN` or tie to 3V3  │
2702e0bb [glm-5.3-flash] #╰──────────────┴──────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────╯
2702e0bb [glm-5.3-flash] #
2702e0bb [glm-5.3-flash] #So four new GPIOs to allocate for CS/DC/RST/BL, and the bus keeps whatever MOSI/SCK your SPI_PORT
2702e0bb [glm-5.3-flash] #already uses.
2702e0bc [glm-5.3-flash] #
2702e0bc [glm-5.3-flash] #Things that change versus your current panel:
2702e0bc [glm-5.3-flash] #
2702e0bc [glm-5.3-flash] #- No MISO — the ST7789 is write-only. Any display readback has to go, and `readSPI()` loses
2702e0bd [glm-5.3-flash] #its only remaining user once touch is gone.
2702e0bd [glm-5.3-flash] #- No touch — the XPT2046 path stays out (it already is). TP_CS/TP_IRQ on 16/17 free up,
2702e0bd [glm-5.3-flash] #which also removes that collision with the `USE_ROM` vector we noted earlier.
2702e0bd [glm-5.3-flash] #- The 240×135 offset quirk — the ST7789's GRAM is 240×320, so landscape orientations need
2702e0be [glm-5.3-flash] #column/row offsets (typically 52/40, varying with MADCTL rotation) or the image lands shifted and
2702e0be [glm-5.3-flash] #wraps. That's driver-side, in wherever `CreatePicoDisplay()` gets its ST7789 init.
2702e0be [glm-5.3-flash] #- Layout won't fit — the ROM pin indicator rects run to x=292 and the spiral reaches x=330,
2702e0bf [glm-5.3-flash] #both past 240. The time text at `LCD_HEIGHT-40` = 95 is fine vertically. Worth reworking those
2702e0bf [glm-5.3-flash] #coordinates while you're in there.
2702e0bf [glm-5.3-flash] #- Your palette code carries over — the byte-swapped RGB565 in `SetColor()` is exactly what
2702e0bf [glm-5.3-flash] #the ST7789 wants over SPI.
2702e0c0 [glm-5.3-flash] #
2702e0c0 [glm-5.3-flash] #One check before you wire it: Waveshare also sell a Pico-LCD-1.14 add-on board that plugs
2702e0c0 [glm-5.3-flash] #directly onto a Pico — that's a different product with a fixed pinout (and four onboard buttons).
2702e0c0 [glm-5.3-flash] #If that's the one you've got, tell me and I'll give you that mapping instead.
