270e8906 [glm-5.3-flash] #Thanks — this one's new to me. It's a Godot 4 diagnostics node that bridges local WebSocket clients
270e8906 [glm-5.3-flash] #(TCP listener on 8080, promoted to `WebSocketPeer` via `accept_stream`) to a single upstream master
270e8906 [glm-5.3-flash] #at `ws://localhost:9000`, with an on-screen `TextEdit` log and an echo handler. A few observations:
270e8906 [glm-5.3-flash] #
270e8907 [glm-5.3-flash] #• Likely bug — the 1K frame counter never fires.* `count&1024==1` can never be true: `count
270e8907 [glm-5.3-flash] #& 1024` only ever yields 0 or 1024, never 1. (Precedence isn't the issue here — `&` binds tighter
270e8907 [glm-5.3-flash] #than `==` in GDScript, so it groups as written.) A modulo check would match the intent.
270e8907 [glm-5.3-flash] #
270e8908 [glm-5.3-flash] #• `sumDelta` is cumulative.* It reports total elapsed time since startup, not per-1K-frame
270e8908 [glm-5.3-flash] #timing. If it's meant as a frame-time diagnostic, divide by 1024 at report time or reset after each
270e8908 [glm-5.3-flash] #report.
270e8908 [glm-5.3-flash] #
270e8909 [glm-5.3-flash] #• No upstream recovery.* Once `masterSocket` reaches `STATE_CLOSED`, nothing reconnects it
270e8909 [glm-5.3-flash] #— `poll()` on a closed peer is inert, so a dropped or failed handshake is permanent for the
270e8909 [glm-5.3-flash] #session. Relatedly, the commented-out `set_process(false)` in `_ready` wouldn't have guarded
270e8909 [glm-5.3-flash] #anything: `connect_to_url` returning `OK` only means the handshake started, and failures surface
270e890a [glm-5.3-flash] #later in `poll`.
270e890a [glm-5.3-flash] #
270e890a [glm-5.3-flash] #• Log growth will dominate at scale.* `log_view.text += ...` per packet is O(n) per append,
270e890a [glm-5.3-flash] #which will become the bottleneck well before the networking does. For a many-to-many load test,
270e890b [glm-5.3-flash] #batching, a capped ring buffer, or throttled flushing would be worth considering.
270e890b [glm-5.3-flash] #
270e890b [glm-5.3-flash] #• Topology note.* Despite the "many to many" header, upstream is a single peer. True
270e890b [glm-5.3-flash] #many-to-many would need a pool of upstream peers managed like the local `sockets` array.
270e890c [glm-5.3-flash] #
270e890c [glm-5.3-flash] #• Positives:* the reverse iteration with `remove_at` during cleanup is correctly done, and
270e890c [glm-5.3-flash] #the accept path is sound.
270e890c [glm-5.3-flash] #
270e890d [glm-5.3-flash] #Minor style points: `@onready` on a `TextEdit.new()` is redundant, `onPacket`'s parameters could be
270e890d [glm-5.3-flash] #typed, and semicolon/spacing use is inconsistent (`"Received"+message` is missing a space).
270e890d [glm-5.3-flash] #
270e890d [glm-5.3-flash] #Happy to sketch a reconnect routine or a capped log approach if you'd like.
270e890e [glm-5.3-flash] #
