270e91b9 [gemini-3.7-flash] #This is a new script. It provides a clean, straightforward continuous rotation for a 3D object
270e91ba [gemini-3.7-flash] #using exported speed properties.
270e91ba [gemini-3.7-flash] #
270e91ba [gemini-3.7-flash] #A couple of technical observations regarding how Godot handles rotations:
270e91ba [gemini-3.7-flash] #
270e91bb [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Local vs. Global Rotation: Calling `rotate_y()` and `rotate_x()` applies transformations
270e91bb [gemini-3.7-flash] #around the node's local coordinate axes in sequence every frame. Because rotating around the local
270e91bb [gemini-3.7-flash] #X-axis tilts the local Y-axis (and vice versa), the object will eventually exhibit a continuous
270e91bb [gemini-3.7-flash] #tumbling precession rather than a fixed-axis turntable rotation. If an independent yaw/pitch or
270e91bc [gemini-3.7-flash] #turntable effect is preferred, rotating around the global Y-axis while pitching on the local X-axis
270e91bc [gemini-3.7-flash] #is often the standard pattern.
270e91bc [gemini-3.7-flash] #• Unused Boilerplate: The default `_ready()` callback with the placeholder comment is
270e91bc [gemini-3.7-flash] #unused and can be removed cleanly if initialization logic is not required.
270e91bd [gemini-3.7-flash] #
270e91bd [gemini-3.7-flash] #Please let me know if you would like any specific adjustments or code examples for different
270e91bd [gemini-3.7-flash] #rotation behaviors.
270e91bd [gemini-3.7-flash] #
