270ea450 [gemini-3.7-flash] #There are three common reasons this happens:
270ea450 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
270ea450 [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. The `TextEdit` UI is covering the viewport:
270ea451 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   If the networking script and the 3D node are running in the same scene, the `log_view`
270ea451 [gemini-3.7-flash] #`TextEdit` control is sized to `1152×648` (default window dimensions). Because UI control nodes
270ea451 [gemini-3.7-flash] #render on top of 3D viewports by default and `TextEdit` is opaque, it completely hides whatever is
270ea451 [gemini-3.7-flash] #rendering behind it.
270ea452 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
270ea452 [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. Missing or poorly positioned `Camera3D`:
270ea452 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   3D geometry requires an active `Camera3D` in the scene to be drawn. Furthermore, because the
270ea452 [gemini-3.7-flash] #cube is 10×10×10 units at the origin `(0, 0, 0)`, a camera placed at default coordinates `(0, 0,
270ea453 [gemini-3.7-flash] #0)` will sit inside the cube. A camera positioned back along the Z-axis (for example, at `(0, 5,
270ea453 [gemini-3.7-flash] #20)`) and pointed toward `(0, 0, 0)` is required to view it.
270ea453 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
270ea453 [gemini-3.7-flash] #3. Active scene tab selection:
270ea454 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   Pressing F6 runs whichever scene tab is currently open and focused in the editor. If the
270ea454 [gemini-3.7-flash] #networking scene tab is active rather than the 3D cube scene, Godot will execute the network
270ea454 [gemini-3.7-flash] #diagnostics scene instead.
270ea454 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
270ea455 [gemini-3.7-flash] #If you would like, I can provide the GDScript to dynamically create and position a `Camera3D` and a
270ea455 [gemini-3.7-flash] #`DirectionalLight3D` automatically within the script.
270ea455 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
