2712f5ce [gemini-3.7-flash] #Thank you for sharing the files. Here are a few notable observations regarding the setup:
2712f5ce [gemini-3.7-flash] #
2712f5ce [gemini-3.7-flash] #1. Type Mismatch in JSON-RPC Response Serialization (`onPacket`)
2712f5cf [gemini-3.7-flash] #   In the diagnostics network script, `response` is defined as a `Dictionary`, and then passed
2712f5cf [gemini-3.7-flash] #directly to `client.send_text(response)`. `WebSocketPeer.send_text()` expects a `String`.
2712f5cf [gemini-3.7-flash] #Converting the dictionary to a string (such as with `JSON.stringify(response)`) before transmission
2712f5cf [gemini-3.7-flash] #will prevent a runtime type error.
2712f5d0 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
2712f5d0 [gemini-3.7-flash] #2. JSON Parsing Guard
2712f5d0 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   If a client sends an empty payload or malformed string, `JSON.parse_string(message)` will return
2712f5d0 [gemini-3.7-flash] #`null` (or a non-dictionary variant). Checking that the parsed result is a valid `Dictionary` prior
2712f5d1 [gemini-3.7-flash] #to calling `.get("id", null)` helps avoid potential runtime exceptions.
2712f5d1 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
2712f5d1 [gemini-3.7-flash] #3. Multiple Script Declarations in a Single Listing
2712f5d1 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   The GDScript snippet contains both `extends Node` and `extends Node3D` within the same block. In
2712f5d2 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Godot, these need to reside in separate `.gd` files or be attached to distinct nodes in your scene
2712f5d2 [gemini-3.7-flash] #tree.
2712f5d2 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
2712f5d2 [gemini-3.7-flash] #4. TypeScript Client Structure
2712f5d2 [gemini-3.7-flash] #   The client cleanly matches the server's expected port (`8080`) and initiates a well-formed
2712f5d2 [gemini-3.7-flash] #JSON-RPC 2.0 `init` handshake on connection with automatic reconnection handling.
2712f5d2 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
2712f5d3 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Please let me know if you would like code adjustments or further details on any of these areas.
2712f5d3 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
