271303f2 [gemini-3.7-flash] #In GDScript, the equivalent of `console.log()` is the built-in function `print()`.
271303f2 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
271303f2 [gemini-3.7-flash] #There are also a few related logging functions available depending on the use case:
271303f2 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
271303f3 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• `print(...)` — Prints the provided arguments to the Godot Output panel and standard
271303f3 [gemini-3.7-flash] #output, separated by spaces.
271303f3 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• `print_debug(...)` — Similar to `print()`, but also appends the current file name, line
271303f3 [gemini-3.7-flash] #number, and stack frame when running in debug mode.
271303f4 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• `print_rich(...)` — Allows BBCode formatting (such as colors and bold text) within the
271303f4 [gemini-3.7-flash] #Godot editor console.
271303f4 [gemini-3.7-flash] #• `printerr(...)` — The equivalent of `console.error()`, directing output to standard error
271303f4 [gemini-3.7-flash] #and formatting it in red within the editor console.
271303f5 [gemini-3.7-flash] #
